hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9601","9574 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, Wa'il ibn Dawud informed me, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Fasting is only from what enters, not from what exits, and ablution is from what exits, not from what enters."
"9602","9575 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abu Sufyan Waki, from Misar, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Amir ibn Mutir al-Shaybani, from his father, he said: We took the pre-dawn meal with Abdullah, then we went out and the prayer was announced."
"9603","9576 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Ibn Masud, he said: When food or drink is offered to one of you while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting."
"9604","9577 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the night of the seventeenth, the morning of Badr, or the twenty-first night, or the twenty-third."
"9605","9578 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, meaning Ubayy ibn Kab, inform me about Laylat al-Qadr, for Ibn Umm Abd says: Whoever stands the whole year will hit it. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; he knew it is in Ramadan, but he concealed it from people so they would not rely on it. By the One Who sent down the Book upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it is indeed in Ramadan, and it is the night of the twenty-seventh. I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us about; we saw it and memorized it. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception. I said to Zirr: What is the sign? He said: The sun rises that morning as though a basin, with no rays."
"9606","9579 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: I said to Ubayy ibn Kab: O Abu al-Mundhir, inform me about Laylat al-Qadr, for our companion Ibn Masud was asked about it and said: Whoever stands the whole year will hit it. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; by Allah, he knew it is in Ramadan, but he disliked that they rely on it - or: he wished they would not rely on it. By Allah, it is indeed in Ramadan, and it is the night of the twenty-seventh; he swears without exception. He said: I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us about. Hammad said: I said to Asim: What is the sign? He said: The sun appears on the morning of that night with no rays, like a basin, until it rises."
"9607","9580 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Zirr, he said: I said to Ubayy: Inform me about Laylat al-Qadr, for Abdullah says: Whoever stands the whole year will hit it. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; he knows it is in Ramadan, but he concealed it from people so they would not rely on it. By Allah, it is the night of the twenty-seventh. I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us of; we counted and memorized that it is indeed it. Asim said: I said to Zirr: What is that sign? He said: The rising of the sun white like a basin, with no rays, until it rises. He said: I watched it repeatedly like that."
"9608","9581 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I met Ubayy ibn Kab - and he was a man in whom there was harshness - and I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, lower your wing for me, may Allah have mercy on you. And I asked him about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: It is in Ramadan, and it is the night of the twenty-seventh. I said: How did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us about; we counted and memorized it. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception."
"9609","9582 - Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hafs al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: Laylat al-Qadr is the night of the twenty-seventh. I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us; I memorized it and counted it. By the One Who sent down the Book upon Muhammad, it is indeed the night of the twenty-seventh."
"9610","9583 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came as a delegate to Uthman, and I met Ubayy ibn Kab and said to him: Narrate to me, for I used to love meeting you, and I came as a delegate only to meet you; narrate to me about Laylat al-Qadr, for Ibn Masud says: Whoever stands the year will hit it - or: will attain it. Ubayy said: He knew it is in Ramadan, but he wished to conceal it from you; it is the night of the twenty-seventh, by the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us; we memorized it and knew it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to keep it alive to the pre-dawn; when it was the day before it and the day after it, he ascended and looked at the sun, and said: The sun rises its morning with no rays until it rises."
"9611","9584 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rawwas narrated to us, Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: A man said to Ubayy ibn Kab: Abdullah ibn Masud says concerning Laylat al-Qadr: Whoever stands the whole year will hit it. Ubayy said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; he knew it is in the month of Ramadan, on the night of the twenty-seventh, but he wished they would not rely on it."
"9612","9585 - Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Ibn Thawban informed us, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: They mentioned Laylat al-Qadr in the presence of Ibn Masud, and he said: Whoever stands the whole month of Ramadan will attain it. He said: I came to Medina and mentioned that to Ubayy, and he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I know which night it is: the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to stand. He said: I asked him about it, and he said: The night of the twenty-seventh. Abdah said: When the month is thirty, we stand three after it, and when it is twenty-nine, we stand two nights after it."
"9613","9586 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Abdullah used to lead us in prayer in the month of Ramadan and would leave deep at night."
"9614","9587 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, he said: I said to Khusayf: Did Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud narrate to you, from his father, that he said: Concerning twenty-five camels, a bint makhad, and if there is none, then an ibn labun, male? He said: Yes."
"9615","9588 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from his father, from Hammam, from Mina, that they came to Abdullah ibn Masud in the time of Uthman and said: Give us our stipends. He said: You have no stipend with me; your stipend is only from your fay and your jizyah, and charity is for its people. When they kept coming back to him, he brought the keys to Uthman, threw them down, and said: I am no treasurer."
"9616","9589 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mujahid, from Ibn Masud, and he was asked about the wealth of orphans. He said: When they come of age, inform them what zakat has become due on it; if they wish, they pay it, and if they wish, they leave it."
"9617","9590 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Masud, he said: The guardian of the orphan counts the years; when he says: He has reached puberty, he says to him: Zakat of such-and-such years is due on you."
"9618","9591 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ibn Masud, he said: He used to give us the stipend, then take its zakat."
"9619","9592 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, he said: A woman asked him about jewelry of hers: Is zakat due on it? He said: When it reaches two hundred dirhams, pay its zakat. She said: There are orphans in my care; shall I give it to them? He said: Yes."
"9620","9593 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that the wife of Ibn Masud said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, is there zakat on my jewelry? He said: Yes. She said: I have orphaned nephews; shall I put it among them? He said: Put it among them."
"9621","9594 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Salamah, from two men between him and Ibn Masud, from Ibn Masud, he said: Whoever earns lawful wealth, withholding zakat makes it impure; and whoever earns unlawful wealth, zakat does not purify it."
"9622","9595 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, both, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Nistas al-Amiri, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: When one of you follows a funeral, let him take hold of all the sides of the bier, for it is of the Sunnah; then let him do voluntary after, or leave. And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Nuaym."
"9623","9596 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: When one of you follows the funeral, let him take hold of all the sides of the bier; then let him do voluntary after, or abandon."
"9624","9597 / 2 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Ibn Masud said: Whoever follows a funeral, let him carry all the sides of the bier, for it is of the Sunnah; then let him do voluntary after, if he wishes."
"9625","9598 - Darran ibn Sufyan al-Attar al-Basri narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: It is of the Sunnah to carry the four sides of the bier; then do voluntary, or leave."
"9626","9599 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Idris al-Kufi, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: It is of the Sunnah to take hold of the four sides of the bier; then do voluntary after, or leave."
"9627","9600 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Ruhayl ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, the like."
"9628","9601 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Misar, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, from Abu Ubaydah, the like."
"9629","9602 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Nakhai narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim said: Abdullah was asked about the washer of the dead: Should he wash? He said: If you mean that your companion is impure, then wash yourselves from him; otherwise, ablution suffices you."
"9630","9603 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, from Alqamah or Masruq, he said: Abdullah said: No saying or recitation was fixed for us over the funeral; say the takbir as the imam says it, and say much of the best speech."
"9631","9604 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Salim al-Barrad, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Masud say: That I step on a live coal is dearer to me than that I step on the grave of a Muslim man."
"9632","9605 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakhai narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: No recitation or saying was fixed for us in prayer over the dead; say the takbir as the imam says it, and say much of the good speech."
"9633","9606 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, he said: Abdullah said: Do not buy fish in the water, for it is uncertainty."
"9634","9607 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: Usury has seventy-odd doors."
"9635","9608 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: Two transactions in one transaction is usury."
"9636","9609 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Ibn Masud, concerning: Divorce them at the commencement of their waiting period: He said: Pure, without intercourse."
"9637","9610 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, concerning: Divorce them for their waiting period: He said: Pure, without intercourse; when he wishes to divorce her according to the Sunnah with three divorces, he divorces her once in purity, then upon her is a menstruation after the last divorce."
"9638","9611 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, he said: Whoever wishes to divorce according to the Sunnah as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded him, let him divorce her pure, without intercourse."
"9639","9612 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas say: Abdullah ibn Masud said, concerning: O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period: He said: Divorce for the waiting period is that you divorce her pure, then leave her until she completes her waiting period, or take her back if you wish. Shubah said: And the people of Kufa say: Without intercourse."
"9640","9613 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: Divorce them for their waiting period: He said: Whoever wishes the divorce that is the divorce, let him wait until, when the woman becomes pure from menstruation, he divorces her pure, without intercourse."
"9641","9614 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: Divorce them for their waiting period: He said: Whoever wishes the divorce that is the divorce, let him leave the woman until, when she becomes pure, without intercourse, he says to her: Observe your waiting period. If he regrets and his soul follows her, he calls two men to witness her return; otherwise he leaves her until her waiting period ends. And let him not divorce her three times while she is pregnant, lest Allah make him regret, so he spends on her pregnancy and her nursing."
"9642","9615 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A woman and her husband came to Umar, and she said: O Commander of the Believers, my husband divorced me, then my blood ceased for three menstruations. Then he came to me after I had put down my water, shut my door, and removed my clothes, and said: I have taken you back, I have taken you back. Umar said to Ibn Masud: What do you think concerning her? He said: I think she is his wife so long as prayer has not become lawful for her. Umar said: And I think that."
"9643","9616 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that he was with Umar ibn al-Khattab when a man and his wife came, and he said: I divorced her then took her back. The woman said: What carried me to narrate the matter as it is, is only what was done to me. Umar said: Tell me. She said: He divorced me, then left me until, when I was at the end of three menstruations, my blood ceased, I put down my washing water, shut my door, and removed my clothes, then he knocked on the door and said: I have taken you back, I have taken you back. So I left my washing and wore my clothes. Umar said: What do you say concerning her, O Ibn Umm Abd? I said: I think he has more right to her so long as prayer has not become lawful for her. Umar said: Good is what you have opined, and I opine that."
"9644","9617 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Umar and Ibn Masud, the like, but he did not mention Alqamah."
"9645","9618 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Zayd ibn Rufay, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Uthman sent to my father asking him about it. My father said: How does a hypocrite give fatwa? Uthman said: We seek refuge for you with Allah from being a hypocrite, and we seek refuge with Allah from calling you a hypocrite, and we seek refuge for you with Allah that the like of this be in Islam then he dies without clarifying it. He said: I think he has more right to her until she washes from the third menstruation and prayer becomes lawful for her. He said: I know of Uthman only that he took that."
"9646","9619 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, that a man divorced his wife once, then she menstruated three menstruations. When she sat to wash, her husband came and took her back. She said: That is not yours. So they raised it to Ibn Masud, and he made her swear by Allah, besides Whom there is no god, that he had indeed taken her back after prayer had become lawful for her; she did not swear, so he returned her to him."
"9647","9620 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Masud, concerning she who is divorced three times before consummation: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. He said: As for al-Thawri, he mentioned it from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, he said: When he divorces three times before consummation, he regarded her as the one consummated with."
"9648","9621 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, concerning a man who divorces his wife three times before consummation: Abdullah used to treat her as the consummated one."
"9649","9622 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim informed me, from the companions of Ibn Masud, from Ibn Masud, that when a woman is divorced while they think menstruation has left her, but that is not clear, she waits a year; if she does not menstruate in it, she observes three months after the year. If she menstruates in the three months, she observes by menstruation; if she menstruates but her menstruation is not complete after she has observed those three months after the year, he said: Do not hasten upon her until you know whether her menstruation is complete or not."
"9650","9623 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, that a man asked Ibn Masud about a man who divorced his wife before consummation: May he marry her daughter? He said: Yes. So he married her and she bore him a child. Then he came to Umar and asked him, and he said: Separate them. He said: She has borne him a child. He said: Even if she bore ten, separate them."
"9651","9624 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ashath, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said concerning the gifted woman: If they accept her, it is one, and she has more right to it; if they do not accept her, it is nothing."
"9652","9625 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: If they accept her, it is one, irrevocable."
"9653","9626 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Waththab narrating, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: When a man says to his wife: Your affair is in your hand, or: Prosper with your affair, or he gifts her to her family and they accept her, then it is one, irrevocable."
"9654","9627 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Qays al-Nakhai narrated to me, he said: A man came to Ibn Masud and said: He divorced his wife last night eight times. He said: Did you say it once? He said: Yes. He said: Do you wish her to be separated? He said: Yes. He said: It is as you said. He said: Then a man came to him and said: He divorced his wife last night as many as the stars. He said: Did you say it once? He said: Yes. He said: Do you wish her to be separated? He said: Yes. He said: It is as you said. Then he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has clarified divorce; whoever divorces as Allah commanded him, it is clarified for him; and whoever confuses himself, we impose his confusion upon him. By Allah, do not confuse yourselves and expect us to bear it for you; it is as you say. He said: And we think a word of Ibn Sirin, which I do not memorize, that he said: Had he the women of the people of the earth, then said this, they would all be gone."
"9655","9628 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: We were with Abdullah ibn Masud when a man came and said: I divorced my wife eight times. Abdullah said: Did you say it once? He said: Yes. He said: Do you wish your wife to be separated from you? He said: Yes. He said: It is as you said. Then a man came to him and said: I divorced my wife as many as the stars. He said: Did you say it once? He said: Yes. He said: Do you wish her to be separated from you? He said: Yes. He said: Abdullah mentioned at that the women of the people of the earth with something I do not memorize, then Abdullah said: Allah has clarified for you how divorce is; whoever divorces as Allah commanded him, it is clarified for him; and whoever is confused, we impose his confusion upon him. By Allah, do not confuse yourselves and expect us to bear it for you; it is as you say."
"9656","9629 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A man came to Ibn Masud and said: I divorced my wife ninety-nine times, and I asked and was told: She is separated from me. Ibn Masud said: They wished to separate you from her. He said: What do you say, may Allah have mercy on you? - thinking he would give him a concession - and he said: Three separate her from you, and the rest is transgression."
"9657","9630 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A man came to Abdullah and said: I divorced my wife ninety times, and I have a child by her, and people wish to separate me from my family. Abdullah said: Three suffice you, and the rest is transgression."
"9658","9631 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that Ibn Masud said: Concerning the unlawful, it is an oath he expiates. Abd al-Razzaq said: As for al-Thawri, he mentioned it from Ashath, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, he said: If he intended divorce, otherwise it is an oath."
"9659","9632 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that Ibn Masud said: Concerning the unlawful, it is the expiation of an oath."
"9660","9633 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, that Umar and Ibn Masud said: Concerning the unlawful, it is the expiation of an oath."
"9661","9634 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: It reached Ibn Abbas that Ibn Masud says: If he divorces what he has not married, it is valid. Ibn Abbas said: He erred in this; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: When you marry believing women then divorce them before touching them - and He did not say: When you divorce believing women, then marry them."
"9662","9635 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: I witnessed Ibn Masud when a man and a woman came to him concerning a prohibition. He said: Allah has clarified; whoever approaches the matter from its right face, it is clarified; and whoever opposes, by Allah, we cannot bear your opposition."
"9663","9636 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Layth, from Wabarah, from a man of them, he said: He took an oath of abstention from his wife for ten days, then asked Ibn Masud about her. He said: If four months pass, it is ila."
"9664","9637 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: al-Numan took an oath of abstention from his wife while he was sitting with Ibn Masud; he struck his thigh and said: When four months pass, acknowledge one divorce."
"9665","9638 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ali, Ibn Masud, and Ibn Abbas said: When the four months pass, it is one divorce, and she has more right to herself. Qatadah said: Ali and Ibn Masud said: She observes the waiting period of the divorced."
"9666","9639 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, and one who heard him narrating informed me, from Mansur, Mughirah, and al-Amash, from Ibrahim, that a man called Abdullah ibn Unays took an oath of abstention from his wife; four months passed before he touched her, then he touched her after the four while not remembering his oath. He came to Alqamah ibn Qays and mentioned that to him, so they came to Ibn Masud and asked him. He said: She is separated from you, so propose to her for herself. So he proposed to her for herself and gave her a ritl of silver as dowry."
"9667","Chapter. 9640 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: Ibn Masud said: Whomever wishes, I shall invoke mutual cursing with him that this verse in the shorter Surah al-Nisa: And those pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden - was revealed after the one in al-Baqarah: And those of you who die and leave wives - the verse. He said: And it reached him that Ali said: It is the later of the two terms, so he said that."
"9668","9641 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, Ibn Shubrumah al-Kufi narrated to me, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Alqamah ibn Qays, that Ibn Masud said: Whomever wishes, I shall invoke mutual cursing with him that: And those pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden - was revealed only after the verse of the widow: And those of you who die and leave wives, they shall wait by themselves four months and ten."
"9669","9642 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Whomever wishes, I shall swear to him that the shorter Surah al-Nisa was revealed after: Four months and ten."
"9670","9643 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (ha) and Yusuf al-Qadi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, both saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, Masruq, and Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: The waiting period of the divorced is from when she is divorced, and of she whose husband dies, from when he dies; and whomever wishes, I shall swear to him that the shorter surah was revealed after al-Baqarah."
"9671","9644 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hilal ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: Whomever wishes, I shall swear to him that the shorter surah was revealed after the long - meaning al-Nisa."
"9672","9645 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Atiyyah, he said: I heard Ibn Masud say: The verse of the shorter: And those pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden - was revealed after the one in al-Baqarah: And those of you who die and leave wives, they shall wait by themselves."
"9673","9646 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Abu Muhammad said: Abu Atiyyah said: They mentioned it from Abdullah, and he said: Her term is that she delivers her burden. The people said: Until four months and ten? Abdullah said: What if four months and ten pass and she has not delivered her burden? They said: Until she delivers. Abdullah said: So you impose the hardship upon her and do not grant her the concession; the verse of the shorter was revealed after the longer: And those pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden. When she delivers her burden, her waiting period ends."
"9674","9647 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: I was in the circle of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, whose companions treated him as an amir, and they mentioned the woman whose husband dies while she is pregnant, so I said: Before the completion of four months and ten. He said: I narrated the hadith of Subayah, from Abdullah ibn Utbah. He said: One of his companions winked at me, so I understood and said: I would indeed be keen on lying if I lied about Abdullah ibn Utbah while he is in the district of Kufa. It was as though he was embarrassed, and he said: But his uncle did not used to say this. He said: I met Malik ibn Amir al-Hamdani and asked him; he began mentioning the hadith of Subayah, so I said: I am not asking you about this; did you hear Ibn Masud say anything concerning it? He said: Yes; they mentioned that in his presence, and he said: What do you say if she delivers before the completion of four months and ten? We said: She waits until the four months and ten pass. He said: What do you say if the four months and ten pass before she delivers? We said: Until she delivers. He said: You impose the hardship upon her and do not grant her the concession; the shorter Surah al-Nisa was revealed after the longer: And those pregnant."
"9675","Chapter. 9648 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, Ibrahim narrated to me, from Alqamah or al-Aswad, that Ibn Masud was approached by a man who said: Between me and my wife was what is between people. She said: If what is in your hand of my affair were in my hand, you would know what I would do. He said: What is in my hand of your affair is in your hand. She said: Then you are divorced three times. He said: I consider it one, and you have more right to return; and I shall meet the Commander of the Believers, Umar. So he met him and told him the story. He said: May Allah do with men, may Allah do with men; they take what Allah placed in their hands and place it in the hands of women - dust in her mouth. What did you say? He said: I said: I consider it one, and he has more right to her. He said: And I opine that; had you opined otherwise, I would have thought you missed. Mansur said: I said to Ibrahim: Ibn Abbas used to say: May Allah confound her course; had she said: I have divorced myself. Ibrahim said: They are the same."
"9676","9649 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: A man came to Ibn Masud and said: Between me and my wife was some speech. She said: If what is of my affair in my hand were in my hand, you would know what I would do. I said: I call you to witness that what is of your affair in my hand is in your hand. She said: Then you are divorced three times. Ibn Masud said: It is one, and you have more right to her; and I shall ask about that the Commander of the Believers. So he rode and met Umar and told him the story. He said: A stone in her mouth; may Allah do with men, may Allah do; they take what Allah placed in their hands of the affair of women and place it in their hands. What do you think? I said: I consider it one, and he has more right to her. He said: Good is what you opined; had you opined otherwise, you would not be right."
"9677","9650 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, that a man placed his wife's affair in her hand, and she divorced herself three times. Ibn Masud was asked what he thought concerning her. He said: I consider it one, and he has more right to her. Umar said: And I opine that."
"9678","9651 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Masud, he said: When he gives her authority over her affair, then they separate before she decides anything, she has no authority."
"9679","9652 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Masud concerning the choice: If she chooses her husband, it is nothing; and if she chooses herself, it is one."
"9680","9653 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar and Ibn Masud said: If she chooses herself, it is one; and if she chooses her husband, it is nothing."
"9681","9654 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Umar and Ibn Masud said concerning: Your affair is in your hand: If she chooses herself, it is one, and he has more right to her; and if she chooses her husband, it is nothing."
"9682","9655 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, he said: Umar and Ibn Masud said: If she chooses her husband, there is no harm; and if she chooses herself, it is one, and he has return over her."
"9683","9656 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Ibn Masud, and he was asked about a man who said to his wife: Choose. She was silent. Then he said to her: Choose. She was silent. Then he said to her the third time: Choose. She said: I have chosen myself. He said: It is three."
"9684","9657 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Women of Hamdan whose husbands were announced dead asked Ibn Masud, and they said: We feel lonely. Abdullah said: Gather by day, then each one of them returns to her house by night."
"9685","9658 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, the like, that he said: Their husbands died in a plague that was in Kufa."
"9686","9659 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ali and Ibn Masud said: If he accuses her after divorcing her while he has return over her, he invokes mutual cursing with her; and if he accuses her after divorcing her irrevocably, he does not invoke mutual cursing with her."
"9687","9660 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The two who invoke mutual cursing never join again."
"9688","9661 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud said: The inheritance of the son of mutual cursing is all for his mother."
"9689","9662 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from a companion of his, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Shabi, from Ali and Ibn Masud, both saying: The agnates of the son of mutual cursing are the agnates of his mother."
"9690","9663 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Ibn Masud was asked about withdrawal, and he said: If Allah took the covenant of a soul in the loins of a man, then he poured it upon a rock, He would bring it out of that rock; if you wish, then complete, and if you wish, then do not practice withdrawal."
"9691","9664 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Ibn Masud, he said concerning withdrawal: It is the hidden buried-alive girl."
"9692","9665 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud disliked joining between two sisters in right-hand possession."
"9693","9666 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud used to dislike the slave woman and her mother together. Qatadah said: A man argued with Ibn Masud concerning joining between two sisters, and said: Allah has made lawful for me what my right hand possesses. He said to him: Your camel is of what your right hand possesses."
"9694","9667 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud said: And I dislike your slave woman as a polytheist."
"9695","9668 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh informed us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Janab al-Kalbi informed us, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from his father, he said: We disputed over the reading of this letter: And He knows what they do - or: you do? So I came to Ibn Masud to ask him about that. While I was with him, a comer came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, a man committed immorality with his wife, then they both repented and set right. Abdullah recited this verse: And He is Who accepts repentance from His servants, pardons evil deeds, and knows what you do."
"9696","9669 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn Masud was asked about a man who commits adultery with a woman, then marries her. He said: They are two adulterers as long as they are together. It was said to Ibn Masud: What if they repent? He said: And He Who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds. Ibn Masud kept repeating it until I said: He sees no harm in it."
"9697","9670 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, he said: I asked Salim ibn Abdullah about a man who commits adultery with a woman then marries her. He said: Ibn Masud was asked about that and said: And He Who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds - the verse."
"9698","9671 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, the like."
"9699","9672 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he said: They are two adulterers as long as they are together."
"9700","9673 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Masud and Aishah, both saying: They remain two adulterers as long as they are together."
"9701","9674 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud used to dislike a man treading his slave woman for immoral gain."
"9702","9675 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, concerning the waiting period of the slave woman, he said: Half the punishment is upon her, and half the concession is not for her."
"9703","9676 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The slave woman is cleared by one menstruation."
"9704","9677 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ashath, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Masud, he said: Divorce and the waiting period are by the woman."
"9705","9678 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: Divorce is by men, and the waiting period is by women."
"9706","9679 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that Ibn Masud said: If she is freed while with a slave, and did not know she has the choice, or was not given the choice until her husband is freed, or until he dies or she dies, they inherit each other."
"9707","9680 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Kanud, he said: Ibn Masud said: The like of one who frees his concubine then marries her is like one who gifts his sacrificial camel then rides it."
"9708","9681 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, concerning the slave woman sold while she has a husband, he said: Her sale is her divorce."
"9709","9682 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Masud, he said: Her sale is her divorce."
"9710","9683 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: A man of us died, leaving a mother of his child. Al-Walid ibn Uqbah wanted to sell her for his debt. So we came to Ibn Masud and found him praying; we waited until he finished his prayer, then mentioned that to him. He said: If you must do it, put her in her child's share."
"9711","9684 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from a shaykh of them, from his father, he said: Jarir ibn Abdullah came to Umar complaining to him of what he meets from women. Umar said: We find that; even I want something and it is said to me: You go only to the young women of so-and-so to look at them. Abdullah ibn Masud said to him at that: Has it not reached you that Ibrahim complained to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, of the sharp character of Sarah, and it was said to him: She was created from a rib, so endure her as she is, so long as you see no disgrace in her religion? Umar said to him: Allah has stuffed much knowledge between your ribs."
"9712","9685 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said concerning the virgin committing adultery with the virgin: They are lashed a hundred each, and exiled a year."
"9713","9686 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, from Amir ibn Matar al-Shaybani, he said: Ibn Masud said concerning a man who takes his wife's slave girl: If he forced her, she is freed and he pays the like of her for her; and if she obeyed him, he keeps her, and pays the like of her for her."
"9714","9687 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Mabad and Ubayd, the two sons of Imran ibn Dhuhl, both saying: Ibn Masud was brought a man who said: I have committed adultery. He said: Then we shall stone you if you were married. They said: He only went to his wife's slave girl. Abdullah said: If you forced her, then free her and give your wife a slave girl in her place. He said: By Allah, I forced her and beat her. So he did not stone him, and ordered him beaten less than the hadd."
"9715","9688 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, that Ibn Masud saw no hadd upon him, nor dower."
"9716","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: Stripping, stretching, shackling, and fettering are not permissible in this ummah."
"9717","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Hammad, from Ibrahim: Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani came to Abdullah and said: A slave-girl of his had committed adultery. He said: Flog her fifty lashes. He said: She has no husband. He said: Her Islam is her chastity."
"9718","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Shurahbil: Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin came to Abdullah and said: He had forbidden himself his bed. Abdullah said: O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you; free a slave. He said: A slave of mine stole a cloak from a slave of mine. He said: Your own wealth stole from itself. He said: My slave-girl committed adultery. He said: Have her flogged. He said: She was never married. He said: Her Islam is her chastity."
"9719","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith: Ibn Muqarrin asked Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I swore not to sleep on my bed for a year. Abdullah recited this verse: O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress; indeed Allah does not love the transgressors. Expiate your oath and sleep on your bed. He said: I am well-off. He said: Free a slave. He said: A slave of mine stole the cloak of a slave of mine. He said: Your wealth stole from itself, meaning there is no amputation for him. He said: My slave-girl committed adultery. He said: Flog her. He said: She was never married. He said: Her Islam is her chastity."
"9720","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from al-A'mash, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud was brought a man found with a woman under one blanket, so he had each of them struck forty lashes and stood them before the people. The families of the woman and the man went and complained of that to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Umar said to Ibn Mas'ud: What do these people say? He said: I did that. He said: Did you deem that right? He said: Yes. They said: We came to him seeking redress, and behold, he was the one questioning him."
"9721","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri and Ma'mar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Ward off the fixed penalties and execution from the servants of Allah as much as you can."
"9722","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim informed me, who said: I was told of Ali and Ibn Mas'ud concerning the virgin coerced against herself: The virgin is due the dower of one like her among women, and the previously married woman is due the dower of one like her."
"9723","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim: Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said concerning the slave-girl who is coerced: If she was a virgin, a tenth of her price is due, and if she was previously married, half a tenth of her price."
"9724","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ali and Ibn Mas'ud, who said: Both a little and a lot of suckling make marriage unlawful."
"9725","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Nakha'i: Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said concerning suckling: Both its little and its much make marriage unlawful."
"9726","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim: Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said: The woman divorced thrice is entitled to lodging and maintenance."
"9727","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I asked Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: When did Abdullah leave Muzdalifah? He said: Like the departure of the people setting out at dawn after the morning prayer."
"9728","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah: Abdullah sent a sacrificial animal with him and said: Eat a third yourself with your companions, give a third in charity, and send a third to the family of my brother Utbah. It was said to Sufyan: A voluntary offering? He said: Yes."
"9729","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I asked Abdullah about a woman who wanted to join an umrah with her hajj, and he said: Have you not heard Allah say: The hajj is in well-known months? I do not regard these as anything but the months of the hajj."
"9730","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from his father, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The impotent husband is given a year; if he consummates with her, well and good, otherwise they are separated."
"9731","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Abdullah, who said: The impotent husband is given a year."
"9732","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' ibn Umaylah informed me, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: The impotent husband is given a year; if he reaches her, well and good, otherwise they are separated, and she keeps the dower."
"9733","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim informed me: Ibn Mas'ud said: Whoever divorces in jest or marries in jest, it is binding."
"9734","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was told of Amir and Masruq and Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to say: Intercourse by her master does not make her lawful for her husband until she marries another husband."
"9735","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah: Ibn Mas'ud said: Allah, mighty and majestic, forbade twelve women, and I dislike twelve: The slave-girl and her mother, two sisters joined together, the slave-girl if your father had intercourse with her, the slave-girl if your son had intercourse with her, the slave-girl if she committed adultery, the slave-girl in the waiting period of another man, the slave-girl who has a husband, your polytheist slave-girl, and your paternal and maternal aunts through suckling."
"9736","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Mas'ud: He gave him nabidh to drink in a green jar. Abu Wa'il said: I have seen that jar."
"9737","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Isra'il, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from the mother of Abu Ubaydah, who said: I used to make nabidh for Abdullah in a green jar while he watched, and he would drink from it."
"9738","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Alqamah ibn Qays, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud was in Syria, and they said to him: Recite for us. So he recited the chapter of Yusuf for us. A man among the people said: It was not revealed like this. Abdullah said: Woe to you, I recited it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to me: You did well. While he was disputing with him, he noticed the smell of wine on him, so Abdullah said: You drink filth and deny the Quran? I will not stand until you are flogged the fixed penalty."
"9739","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: I recited in Hims, and a man said: It was not revealed like this. I drew near him and noticed the smell of wine on him, so I said: You deny the truth and drink filth? By Allah, this is how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me. I will not leave you until I strike you the fixed penalty. He said: So he struck him the fixed penalty."
"9740","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, who said: A man among us named Khuthaym ibn Adda' complained of his stomach, and sukkar was soaked for him. Abdullah said: Allah, mighty and majestic, would not place your cure in what He forbade you."
"9741","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, likewise. Ma'mar said: Sukkar comes from dates mixed with something."
"9742","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur and Asim, from Abu Wa'il, who said: A man among us complained, and sukkar was prescribed for him. We came to Abdullah and asked him, and he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has not placed your cure in what He forbade you."
"9743","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad ibn Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Do not give your children to drink; they were born upon the natural disposition. Would you give them to drink what is not lawful for them? Their sin is upon whoever gives them. Allah, mighty and majestic, has not placed your cure in what He forbade you."
"9744","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: Those who fall from mountaintops, whom beasts devour, and who drown in seas are martyrs with Allah."
"9745","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from al-Qasim, who said: Ibn Mas'ud was asked about a man who freed his slave at death while having no wealth besides him and owing a debt. He said: He labors to pay his price."
"9746","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: A man came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: A slave-girl of mine suckled a son of mine, and I want to sell her. Ibn Mas'ud rebuked him and said: Would that he would announce: The one I sell is the mother of my child."
"9747","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri and Isra'il, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salamah, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud bought a slave-girl from a man for six hundred, or nine hundred, and sought him for a year without finding him. Then he went out with her price to the open ground and gave it in charity, dirham by dirham, on behalf of her owner. If her owner comes, he gives him the choice: if he chooses the reward, it is his, and if he chooses his money, his money is his. Ibn Mas'ud said: Do thus with lost property. The wording is that of Abd al-Razzaq's hadith."
"9748","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Sinan al-Asadi, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: Those two bitter ones are withholding in life and squandering at death."
"9749","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysarah al-Hamdani Amr ibn Shurahbil, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said to me: You are among the most likely quarters in Kufa for one of you to die leaving neither agnate nor kin; what prevents him, being so, from placing his wealth among the poor or needy."
"9750","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah ibn Zufar, who said: A man of Hamdan came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud on a piebald horse and said: My uncle entrusted his estate to me, and this is from his estate; shall I buy it? He said: No, and do not borrow anything from their wealth."
"9751","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from a man, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud when a man of Hamdan came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, shall I buy this horse? He said: What is its case? He said: Its owner entrusted it to me. He said: Do not buy it, and do not borrow anything from his wealth."
"9752","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla informed me: Ibn Mas'ud said: Quasi-intentional killing is with stone, stick, whip, a push, a shove, and everything you intend with it; therein is aggravation of the blood-money. And error is that one shoots at a thing and misses with it."
"9753","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim informed me, from Ali and Ibn Mas'ud: Quasi-intentional killing is with stone and stick."
"9754","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abd al-Karim informed me, from Ali and Ibn Mas'ud, who said: There is aggravation in quasi-intentional killing, but no execution for it."
"9755","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim: Ibn Mas'ud said: Quasi-intentional killing is twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadha'ah, twenty-five bint makhad, and twenty-five bint labun."
"9756","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim: Ibn Mas'ud said: In error, in fifths: twenty hiqqah, twenty jadha'ah, twenty banat makhad, twenty ibn makhad, and twenty bint labun."
"9757","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj: Alqamah ibn Qays said: Ibn Mas'ud said: For every pair there is the full blood-money, and for every single one there is the full blood-money."
"9758","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from al-Sha'bi: Ibn Mas'ud said: The two eyes are equal, the two testicles are equal, the fingers are equal, the teeth are equal, the two hands are equal, and the two feet are equal."
"9759","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid: Ibn Mas'ud said concerning the man and the woman: They are equal up to five camels. He said: And Ali said: Half of everything."
"9760","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Sa'id, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said, concerning the man from whom retaliation is taken and then he dies: It is upon the one who exacted retaliation from his blood-money, then the blood-money for his wound is deducted from it."
"9761","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah: A man who had killed a man was brought before Umar ibn al-Khattab, and the children of the slain came, one of them having pardoned. Umar said to Ibn Mas'ud, who was beside him: What do you say? Ibn Mas'ud said: I say to him: He is now protected from execution. He said: So he struck his shoulder and said: A small vessel filled with knowledge."
"9762","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from one of his companions, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Ibn Mas'ud, concerning one who incurs fixed penalties then is deliberately killed: When execution comes, it wipes away everything."
"9763","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: Ibn Mas'ud said: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"9764","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The blood-money of the covenanted one is like the blood-money of the Muslim. And Ali said so too."
"9765","Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Abi Najih informed me, from Mujahid, reporting from Ibn Mas'ud, that he said: For every covenanted person, Magian or otherwise, the blood-money is complete."
"9766","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim: Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin asked Ibn Mas'ud and said: A slave-lad of mine stole a cloak from a slave-lad of mine; is there amputation for him? He said: No; your wealth is one part from another."
"9767","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: It was said to Ibn Mas'ud: Will you deal with al-Walid ibn Uqbah, whose beard drips with wine? He said: We have been forbidden spying; if it becomes manifest to us, meaning, we will impose it upon him."
"9768","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The hand is not cut except for a dinar or ten dirhams."
"9769","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah said: The hand is not cut except for a dinar or ten dirhams."
"9770","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: The shroud comes from the whole of the wealth."
"9771","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed a disbeliever. Al-Mas'udi did not say: from his father."
"9772","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed a disbeliever. Isra'il did not raise it, while Sharik raised it."
"9773","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, and Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us, both saying: Ishaq ibn al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill snakes; whoever fears their retaliation is not from me."
"9774","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Farra', from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The Muslim owes the Muslim six acts of kindness: he greets him when he meets him, answers him when he invites him, says yarhamuk Allah when he sneezes, attends him when he dies, advises him in his absence, and loves for him what he loves for himself. Abu Ja'far al-Farra' did not raise it, while Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i raised it."
"9775","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah, who said: A time will come upon people when a man will come to the grave and say: Would that I were in the place of its occupant; not out of love for meeting Allah, but because of the affliction he sees."
"9776","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah, who said: A time will surely come upon you when a man will pass by the grave and say: Would that I were in the place of this one; not out of love for meeting Allah, but due to the severity of the affliction he sees. It was said: What thing is best then? He said: A strong horse and a weapon with which a man moves wherever he moves."
"9777","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah, who said: For a camel smeared with tar to crowd me is dearer to me than for a perfumed woman to crowd me."
"9778","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', who said: Abdullah said: For a man to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"9779","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', who said: Abdullah said: Keep the Quran unmixed; do not clothe it with what is not of it."
"9780","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah, who said: The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing you will lose of your religion is prayer."
"9781","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah, who said: The Trumpet is like the shape of a horn, blown into."
"9782","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', who said: Abdullah said: Mix with people yet keep apart from them."
"9783","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: Mix with people and humor them in what they desire, but your religion, do not impair it."
"9784","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah: A man had wealth in which he had never done any good at all, and when death came to him he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then scatter me in the wind. That was done with him, and Allah gathered him and said: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Out of fear of You. So the mercy of Allah reached him."
"9785","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', who said: Abdullah said: Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will not guide you when they have misguided themselves; either they tell you truth and you deny them, or falsehood and you believe them."
"9786","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Abu al-Za'ra', from Abdullah, that he mentioned intercession and said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will stand fourth of four. Shu'bah said: I heard this only in this hadith."
"9787","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra', who said: The Dajjal was mentioned before Abdullah, and he said: You people will split into three groups: a group following him, a group joining the land of their forefathers, the wormwood-growing places, and a group taking the bank of this Euphrates, fighting him while he fights them, until the believers gather west of Syria. They will send a scout party to him, among them a horseman on a reddish or piebald horse, and they will be killed, none returning to them. He said: And Abu Sadiq narrated to me, from Rabi'ah ibn Najid, from Abdullah, who said: A reddish horse. Abdullah said: And the People of the Book claim that the Messiah will descend and kill him, though I never heard him narrate a hadith from the People of the Book other than this. Then Gog and Magog will emerge, surging through the land and corrupting therein. Then Abdullah recited: And they from every elevation hasten down. Then Allah will send upon them a creature like this worm, entering their ears and nostrils, and they will die, and the earth will stink from them. He said: The earth will cry out to Allah, and Allah will send water purifying the earth of them. Then Allah will send a wind with intense cold, leaving no believer upon the face of the earth but taken by that wind. Then the Hour will stand over the worst of people. Then an angel will stand with the Trumpet between heaven and earth and blow into it, and no creature of Allah in the heavens and earth will remain but die, except whom your Lord wills. Then between the two blows will be whatever Allah wills it to be. He said: There is no created being of the sons of Adam but something of him remains in the earth. Then Allah will send water from beneath the Throne, gushing like the fluid of men, and their bodies and flesh will grow from that water as the earth grows from soil. Then Abdullah recited: He who sent the winds stirring clouds, and We drove it to a dead land and revived thereby the earth after its death; thus is the resurrection. Then an angel will stand with the Trumpet between heaven and earth and blow into it, and every soul will hasten to its body until entering it, and they will rise living the life of one man, standing for the Lord of the worlds. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, will present Himself to creation and meet them; and there is none of creation worshipping anything besides Allah but it will rise before him followed by him. He will meet the Jews and say: What did you worship? They will say: Uzayr. He will say: Would water please you? They will say: Yes. He will show them Hell like a mirage. Then Abdullah recited: And We will present Hell that Day to the disbelievers, displayed. Then He will meet the Christians and say: What did you worship? They will say: The Messiah. He will say: Would drink please you? They will say: Yes. He will show them Hell like a mirage, and likewise for whoever worshipped anything besides Allah. Then Abdullah recited: And stop them; indeed they are to be questioned. Until the Muslims pass, and He will meet them and say: Whom do you worship? They will say: We worship Allah, associating nothing with Him. He will rebuke them once or twice: Whom do you worship? They will say: Glory be to Him; when He discloses Himself to us, we will know Him. At that, the shin will be uncovered, and no believer will remain but fall prostrate to Allah, while the hypocrites remain, their backs one slab as though safflower stakes were in them. They will say: Our Lord. He will say: You used to be called to prostration while sound. Then He will command the bridge, and it will be laid over Hell. People will pass by their deeds in crowds: the first of them like the blink of lightning, then like the passing of wind, then like the passing of birds, then like the swiftest of beasts. He said: Then likewise until a man comes hastening, until a man comes walking, until the last of them is a man dragged upon his belly, saying: My Lord, You delayed me. He will say: Your deed delayed you. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, will permit intercession. The first intercessor on the Day of Resurrection will be Gabriel, then Abraham, then Moses, or he said Jesus, peace be upon them. Salamah said: Then your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will stand fourth; none after him will intercede in what he intercedes in. It is the Praised Station Allah promised him: Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praised station. And there is no soul but looks at a house in Paradise and a house in Hell, and it will be said: Had you acted. It is the Day of Regret. He said: The people of Hell will see the house in Paradise, and it will be said: Had you acted; and the people of Paradise will see the house in Hell and say: Had Allah not favored you. Then the angels, the prophets, the martyrs, the righteous, and the believers will intercede, and Allah will grant them intercession. Then He will say: I am the Most Merciful of the merciful, and He will bring out of Hell more than all creation brought out, by His mercy, until leaving therein none in whom is good. Then Abdullah recited: Say, O disbelievers: What put you into Saqar; and he knotted with his hand: They will say: We were not of those who prayed, nor did we feed the poor, and we used to enter into vain discourse with those who engaged therein, and we used to deny the Day of Recompense; and he knotted four, Sufyan said: with his hand, joining four fingers, and Abu Nu'aym described it. Then Abdullah said: Do you see among these any in whom is good? When Allah wills that none come out of it, He will change their faces and colors. A man of the believers will come to intercede, and it will be said to him: Whoever knows anyone, let him bring him out. The man will come and look, knowing no one. The man will say to the man: O so-and-so, I am so-and-so. He will say: I do not know you. They will say: Our Lord, bring us out of it; if we return, we are wrongdoers. He will say: Remain despised therein and do not speak to Me. When He says that, it will be sealed over them, and no human will come out of them."
"9788","Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam and Abu Hanifah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Za'ra': Abdullah said: Allah, mighty and majestic, will punish a people of the people of faith, then bring them out by the intercession of the intercessors. Then he said: These are those whom the intercession of the intercessors will not benefit."
"9789","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abu Ubaydah, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud:"
"9790","And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda', Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah will gather the first and the last for the appointment of a known Day, standing forty years, their gazes fixed toward heaven, awaiting the decisive judgment. He said: And Allah, mighty and majestic, will descend in shades of cloud, from the Throne to the Footstool. Then a caller will call: O people, are you not content with your Lord who created you, sustained you, and commanded you to worship Him and associate nothing with Him, that He entrusts each people among you to what they used to take as patrons and worship in religion? Is that not justice from your Lord? They will say: Yes indeed. He said: Let every people go to what they used to worship in the world. He said: They will go, and there will appear to them likenesses of what they worshipped: some will go to the sun, some to the moon, and to idols of stone and the like of what they worshipped. He said: And there will appear, for whoever worshipped Jesus, the devil of Jesus, and for whoever worshipped Uzayr, the devil of Uzayr, while Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his ummah remain. He said: The Lord, mighty and majestic, will present Himself and come to them, saying: What is with you that you do not go as the people went? They will say: We have a God we have not yet seen. He will say: Would you know Him if you saw Him? They will say: Between us and Him is a sign; when we see it, we will know it. He will say: What is it? They will say: The shin will be uncovered. He said: At that the shin will be uncovered, and everyone whose back was a slab will fall down, while a people will remain, their backs like the horns of cows, wanting prostration but unable, though they used to be called to prostration while sound. Then He will say: Raise your heads. They will raise their heads and He will give them their light according to their deeds: some given light like a great mountain hastening before them, some given less than that, some given light like a palm tree at his right, some given less than that, until a man is given his light upon the nail of his foot, shining once and fading once; when it shines he steps forward and walks, and when it is extinguished he stands. He said: The Lord, mighty and majestic, will be before them until passing through the Fire, its trace remaining like the edge of a sword, a slippery place of stumbling. He said: And He will say: Pass. They will pass according to their light: some passing like the blink of an eye, some like lightning, some like a cloud, some like a falling star, some like wind, some like the stride of a horse, some like the stride of a man, until the one given his light upon the nail of his feet crawls upon his face, hands, and feet, one leg falling and one leg catching, the Fire striking his sides, remaining thus until freed. When freed he will stand upon it and say: Praise be to Allah; Allah has given me what He gave none, saving me from it after seeing it. He said: He will be taken to a pond at the gate of Paradise and bathe, and the scent and colors of the people of Paradise will return to him. He will see what is in Paradise through the gate and say: My Lord, admit me to Paradise. Allah will say to him: Do you ask for Paradise when I have saved you from the Fire? He will say: My Lord, place between me and it a veil so I hear not its sound. He said: He will enter Paradise. He said: He will see, or there will be raised for him, a dwelling ahead of that as though a dream toward it, and say: My Lord, give me that dwelling. He will say to him: Perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask for other. He will say: No, by Your might, I will ask You for no other; what dwelling could be fairer than it. He said: And he will see, or there will be raised for him, ahead of that another dwelling as though a dream toward it, and say: Give me that dwelling. Allah, exalted be His majesty, will say: Perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask for other. He will say: No, by Your might, I will ask for no other; what dwelling could be fairer than it. He said: He will be given it and descend therein, then fall silent. Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: What is with you that you do not ask? He will say: My Lord, I have asked You until I am shy of You, and sworn to You until I am shy of You. Allah, exalted, will say: Are you not content that I give you the like of the world since I created it until the day I ended it, and tenfold with it? He will say: Do You mock me while You are Lord of might? The Lord, mighty and majestic, will laugh at his saying. He said: I saw Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, when he reached this place of this hadith, laugh. A man said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have heard you narrate this hadith many times; each time you reach this place you laugh. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrate this hadith many times; each time he reached this place of this hadith he laughed until his molars showed. He said: The Lord, mighty and majestic, will say: But I am over that capable; ask. He will say: Join me with the people. He will say: Join the people. He said: He will go hastening in Paradise until, when near the people, a palace of pearl will be raised for him, and he will fall prostrate. It will be said to him: Raise your head; what is with you? He will say: I saw my Lord, or my Lord appeared to me. It will be said to him: It is but a dwelling of your dwellings. He said: Then he will meet a man and prepare to prostrate to him, and it will be said to him: Stop; what is with you? He will say: I thought you an angel of the angels. He will say: I am but a treasurer of your treasurers, a servant of your servants, under my hand a thousand stewards upon the like of what I am upon. He said: He will go ahead of him until the palace is opened for him. He said: It is of hollow pearl, its roofs, doors, locks, and keys of it; a green jewel lined with red will meet him, each jewel leading to a jewel of unlike color; in each jewel are couches, spouses, and maidens, the least of them a wide-eyed houri upon her seventy robes, the marrow of her leg seen from behind her robes, her liver his mirror and his liver her mirror; when he turns from her a turning, she increases in his eye seventyfold over what she was, and when she turns from him a turning, he increases in her eye seventyfold over what he was. He will say to her: By Allah, you have increased in my eye seventyfold. She will say to him: By Allah, you have increased in my eye seventyfold. It will be said to him: Overlook. He said: He will overlook. It will be said to him: Your dominion is a hundred years' journey, pierced by your sight. He said: Umar said: Do you not hear what Ibn Umm Abd narrates to us, O Ka'b, of the lowest of the people of Paradise in station; how then of their highest? Ka'b said: O Commander of the Faithful: What no eye has seen nor ear heard; Allah, mighty and majestic, made a house placing therein what He willed of spouses, fruits, and drinks, then sealed it, then none of His creation saw it, neither Gabriel nor other angels. Then Ka'b recited: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of eyes as reward for what they used to do. He said: And He created below that two Gardens, adorning them with what He willed and showing them to whom He willed of His creation. Then He said: Whoever's book is in Illiyyun will descend that house none has seen, so that a man of the people of Illiyyun will go out walking in his dominion, and no tent of the tents of Paradise will remain but entered by the light of his face, and they will rejoice at his scent, saying: Ah, this scent; this is a man of the people of Illiyyun, gone out walking in his dominion. He said: Woe to you, O Ka'b; these hearts have run loose, restrain them. Ka'b said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Hell will have a moan on the Day of Resurrection; no near angel nor sent prophet but falls to his knees, so that Ibrahim, the friend of Allah, will say: My Lord, myself, myself; even if you had the deeds of seventy prophets added to your deed, you would think you will not escape. And the wording is that of the hadith of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"9791","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Warqa' ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu Taybah narrated to us, from Kurz ibn Wabarah, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will stand for the Lord of the worlds forty years, their gazes fixed, awaiting the decisive judgment, until sweat overwhelms them from severe distress. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, will descend, the nations will kneel, and He will call: O people, are you not content with your Lord who created you and commanded you with His worship, then you turned away from Him and denied His favor, that He leaves you to what you took as patrons? Each man takes charge of what he took charge of. A caller will call: Whoever took charge of a thing, let him keep to it. He said: Whoever took charge of a stone, a tree, or a beast will go. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"9792","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: We talked one night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until talk wearied us. In the morning we went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The prophets were shown to me with their followers from their nations: a prophet with a large company of his nation, and a prophet with no one with him; Allah has told you of the people of Lut, saying: Is there not among you a right-minded man. He said: Until Musa ibn Imran (peace be upon him) passed, with those of the Children of Isra'il with him. I said: My Lord, where is my nation? He said: Look to your right. The hills, the hills of Mecca, were blocked with the faces of men. He said: Are you content, O Muhammad? I said: I am content, my Lord. He said: Look to your left. I looked, and the horizon was blocked with the faces of men. He said: Are you content, O Muhammad? I said: I am content, my Lord. He said: With these are seventy thousand entering Paradise without reckoning. Ukkashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi came and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me of them. He said: O Allah, make him of them. Then another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah to make me of them. He said: Ukkashah beat you to it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: If you can, may my father and mother be ransom for you, be of the seventy, then be so; if you are unable and fall short, be of the companions of the hills; if you are unable and fall short, be of the companions of the horizon, for I have seen many people crowding. Then he said: I hope those following me of my nation will be a quarter of Paradise. The people said Allahu akbar. Then he said: I hope they will be half the people of Paradise. The people said Allahu akbar. Then he recited this verse: A company of the former peoples and a few of the later. They discussed among themselves: Who are these seventy thousand? Some said: A people born in Islam dying upon it. The talk was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: They are those who do not seek ruqyah, do not take omens, and trust in their Lord."
"9793","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: They talked much with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, then we went to him in the morning, and he said: The prophets with their nations were shown to me: a prophet passing with a large company, a prophet with a band, a prophet with a few, and a prophet with no one with him, until Musa, peace be upon him, passed with a great multitude of the Children of Isra'il, and they pleased me. I said: Who are these? It was said: This is your brother Musa, with the Children of Isra'il. I said: Where is my nation? It was said: Look to your right. I looked, and the hills were blocked with the faces of men. Then it was said to me: Look to your left. I looked, and the horizon was blocked with the faces of men. It was said to me: Are you content? I said: I am content, my Lord, I am content, my Lord. It was said to me: With these are seventy thousand entering Paradise without reckoning. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May my father and mother be ransom for you; if you can be of the seventy thousand, do so; if you fall short, be of the people of the hills; if you fall short, be of the people of the horizon, for I have seen people crowding. Ukkashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi stood and said: Supplicate for me, O Messenger of Allah, that He make me of the seventy. He supplicated for him. Another man stood and said: Supplicate Allah, O Messenger of Allah, to make me of them. He said: Ukkashah beat you to it. He said: Then we talked, saying: Who are these seventy thousand? A people born in Islam until they died? That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: They are those who do not brand with cautery, do not seek ruqyah, do not take omens, and trust in their Lord."
"9794","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: We talked with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he mentioned the like of Ma'mar's hadith."
"9795","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9796","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9797","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu Umayyah al-Habati narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Ala' ibn Ziyad, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9798","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Hanash, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, from Ibn Mas'ud: He was in an orchard of the orchards of Medina, teaching his two sons, when two birds passed him, two crows or two pigeons, fluttering. Ibn Mas'ud looked at them and said: By Allah, I am no more grieved for these two were they to die than my grief for these two birds were they to fall dead; I feel for them what a father feels for his child. But I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour will not stand until the hypocrites of every tribe lead it; so I wished to die before that time."
"9799","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, both saying: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Qays al-Rahabi narrated to us, Ata' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The foot of the son of Adam will not move on the Day of Resurrection from before his Lord until asked about five: about his life, in what he spent it; his youth, in what he wore it out; his wealth, from where he earned it and in what he spent it; and what he did with what he knew."
"9800","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub informed us, Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud informed him that there were only four years between their Islam and the revelation of this verse by which Allah reproached them: And let them not be like those given the Book before, for whom the term was prolonged and their hearts hardened, and many of them are defiantly disobedient."
"9801","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from Amr ibn Wabisah al-Asadi, from his father, who said: I was in Kufa in my house when I heard at the door: Peace be upon you, may I enter? I said: Upon you be peace, enter. When he entered, behold, it was Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what a time for a visit this is? That was near midday. He said: The day grew long for me, and I remembered one to talk with. He said: He began telling me of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I told him. Then he began telling me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a tribulation in which the sleeper is better than the recliner, the recliner better than the sitter, the sitter better than the stander, the stander better than the walker, the walker better than the rider, and the rider therein better than the galloper; all its slain are in the Fire. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when is that? He said: That is in the days of harj. I said: When are the days of harj? He said: When a man does not trust his companion. I said: What do you command me if I reach that time? He said: Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if one enters upon me in my house? He said: Enter your room. I said: What if one enters upon me in my room? He said: Enter your mosque, do thus, and he gripped his right hand upon his wrist, and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die thus."
"9802","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last to enter Paradise will walk upon the bridge, walking once and stumbling once, scorched by the Fire. When he passes it, he will turn to it and say: Blessed is He who saved me from you; He has given me what He gave none of the first and the last. A tree will be raised for him, and he will say: My Lord, bring me near this tree, to shade in its shade and drink of its water. Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: O son of Adam, perhaps if I give it to you, you will ask Me for other than it? He will bring him near it, his Lord knowing he will do so. He will shade in its shade and drink of its water. Then another tree will be raised for him, fairer than the first, and he will say: My Lord, bring me near it, to shade in its shade and drink of its water, and I will not ask You for other than it, his Lord knowing he will do so, for he sees what he cannot bear. Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: O son of Adam, did you not covenant Me not to ask Me for other than it? He will say: Yes indeed, my Lord, but this one, I will not ask You for other than it, his Lord knowing he will do so, excusing him, for he sees what he cannot bear. Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: Perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for other than it? He will covenant Him not to do so, and He will bring him near it. He will shade in its shade and drink of its water. Then a tree will be raised for him at the gate of Paradise, fairer than the first two, and he will say: My Lord, bring me near this one, to shade in its shade and drink of its water. Allah, exalted be His remembrance, will say: O son of Adam, did you not covenant Me not to ask Me for other than it? He will say: Yes indeed, my Lord, bring me near this one; perhaps if You bring me near it, I will not ask You for other than it. His Lord will excuse him, for He sees what he cannot bear, and bring him near it. He will hear the voices of the people of Paradise and say: My Lord, admit me into it. He will say: O son of Adam, would you be content that I give you the world and its like with it? He will say: Do You mock me while You are Lord of the worlds? The Messenger of Allah laughed, then said: Will you not ask me why I laughed? He said: Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: At the laughter of the Lord of the worlds, blessed and exalted, when he said: Do You mock me while You are Lord of the worlds? He will say: No, I do not mock, but I am over whatever I will, capable."
"9803","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The deeds of the sons of Adam are presented every Monday and every Thursday; He has mercy on the merciful and forgives the seekers of forgiveness, then leaves the spiteful to their spite."
"9804","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A time will surely come upon people when you will envy a man for lightness of burden as today you envy him for much wealth and children, until one of you passes the grave of his brother and rolls upon it as a beast rolls in its pasture, saying: Would that I were in his place; not from longing for Allah, nor any righteous deed put forth, but from the affliction descending upon him."
"9805","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the servant prays without completing its humility or its bowing, and glances much, it is not accepted from him; and whoever drags his garment in pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, though he be noble to Allah."
"9806","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wears silk in the world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"9807","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to me, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Hajjaj, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is with whom he loves."
"9808","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, Ma'n narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Hurayth, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was over them a witness as long as I remained among them."
"9809","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl al-Ansari, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja' al-Sulami, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us with prayer at the eclipse of the sun and moon; when you see it befall them, hasten to prayer, for if it be what you fear, you will be in no heedlessness, and if it be not, you will have attained good and earned it."
"9810","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Ya'la al-Tawwazi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja' al-Makki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I passed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he signaled to me."
"9811","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Fudayl al-Khatmi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet but he had disciples, guided by his guidance and following his practice; then after them will be successors saying what they do not do and doing what you deny. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer; beyond that there is not of faith a mustard seed's weight."
"9812","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is struck by need and brings it to people, his poverty will not be closed; if he brings it to Allah, mighty and majestic, Allah will soon grant him riches, either deferred reward or prompt riches."
"9813","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Asim ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to me, my father narrated to me, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Ma'n al-Raqashi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Bashir Abu Isma'il, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9814","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Sulayman, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour has drawn near, and they only grow in distance from it."
"9815","Ubayd al-Ujayli narrated to us, Abu Hassan al-Razi narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Rukayn, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Treat with cows' milk, for I hope Allah places healing in it, for it eats of trees."
"9816","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Umar Abu Hafs narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim says, upon hearing the call to prayer, magnifying and bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, then says: O Allah, grant Muhammad the Wasilah, and make his rank among the highest, his love among the chosen, and his remembrance among the near, but intercession will be due him on the Day of Resurrection."
"9817","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Taymi Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when angry, his cheeks reddened."
"9818","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Qays ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, is with the judge, so long as he does not deliberately wrong."
"9819","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, who said: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Bahili narrating from his father, who had companionship, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I think Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to delay the noon prayer for coolness, for heat is of the blast of Hell."
"9820","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Madrabah and from others, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of prayer in the midday heat, and he did not relieve us."
"9821","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Junadah ibn Salm narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Utbah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you fears the ruler, let him say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the mighty Throne, be my protector from the evil of so-and-so son of so-and-so, meaning the one he intends, and from the evil of jinn and men and their followers, lest any of them transgress against me; mighty is Your protection, exalted is Your praise, and there is no god but You."
"9822","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala' al-Himsi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him: A rooster crowed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man said: O Allah, curse it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse it nor revile it, for it calls to prayer."
"9823","Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Mihsan ibn Ali, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The rememberer of Allah among the heedless is like the steadfast among the fleeing."
"9824","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Ma'bad al-Rummani, from Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: It was revealed concerning a party of Arabs who worshipped a party of jinn; the jinn became Muslim while the party of Arabs knew not, concerning His saying: Those whom they call seek the means to their Lord."
"9825","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from Hammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believing servant whose eyes shed tears, though like the head of a fly, from fear of Allah, but Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"9826","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nearest of people to me on the Day of Resurrection are those most invoking blessings upon me."
"9827","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Zaynab the wife of Abdullah, from Abdullah, I know it only as raised: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt, and she shall not stipulate the divorce of her sister to overturn what is in her bowl."
"9828","A chapter. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah Amr ibn Abdullah al-Nakha'i narrated to us, Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrated to us, the master of this house narrated to me, meaning Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its appointed time. I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Kindness to parents. I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: That people be safe from your tongue. Then he fell silent; had I asked more, he would have given me more."
"9829","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to me, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Amr ibn Abdullah al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9830","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar narrated to me, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time. I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then kindness to parents. I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Striving in the path of Allah. Then he fell silent; had I asked more, he would have given me more."
"9831","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, who said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani, the master of this house narrated to me, meaning Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? Or: Which deed is most beloved to Allah? He said: Prayer at its time. I said: Then which? He said: Kindness to parents. I said: Then which? He said: Then striving in the path of Allah. Had I asked more, he would have given me more."
"9832","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, both from al-Shaybani, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time, then striving in the path of Allah."
"9833","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time, then kindness to parents, then striving in the path of Allah."
"9834","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deed is best? He said: Prayer at the beginning of its time, kindness to parents, and striving in the path of Allah."
"9835","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Bayan narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time. It was said: Then which? He said: Kindness to parents. It was said: Then which? He said: Striving in the path of Allah."
"9836","Sulayman ibn al-Husayn al-Attar al-Basri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Sulayman, who said: Abu Amr al-Shaybani mentioned, the lord of this house informed me, meaning Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its appointed time. I said: Then which? He said: Kindness to parents. I said: Then which? He said: Striving in the path of Allah. Then he fell silent toward me; had I asked more, he would have given me more."
"9837","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr: Ibn Mas'ud said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Establishing prayer at its time, kindness to parents, and striving in the path of Allah. I said: Which deed is worst? He said: To set up a rival for your Creator, to kill your child lest he eat with you, or to commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. And the Quran was revealed."
"9838","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Suda'i narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, who said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and said: Which deeds are best? He said: You ask me of what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about. He said: Prayer at its time, kindness to parents, and striving in the path of Allah. Had I asked more, he would have given me more."
"9839","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Prayer at its time."
"9840","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ubayd al-Muktib, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time."
"9841","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Jami' al-Sukkari narrated to us, Amr ibn Jarir al-Bajali narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: A people came to him asking of virtues, and he said: The prescribed prayer at its time, and kindness to parents."
"9842","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Wadih al-Assal al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Mu'ammar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, and Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Sinan ibn Muzahir narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Ja'far al-Farra' narrated to us, and Abu Sayyar Ahmad ibn Hammuwayh al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yazid al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Hamdan ibn Musa al-Tustari al-Abbadani narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak al-Kindi narrated to us, all of them from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: The prayers at their times, kindness to parents, and striving in the path of Allah. The wording is that of Ma'mar's hadith, the others likewise."
"9843","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah and Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time, kindness to parents, and striving in the path of Allah. Had I asked more, he would have given me more."
"9844","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban and Abu Awanah narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim informed us, all of them from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: That you pray the prayer at its appointed times. He said: Then what? He said: Kindness to parents. He said: Then what? He said: Striving in the path of Allah. Had I asked more, he would have given me more. The wording is that of Ibrahim ibn Tahman's hadith, the others likewise."
"9845","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah al-Kalbi narrated to us, saying: I heard Awn ibn Abdullah say: I asked al-Aswad ibn Yazid: Did Ibn Mas'ud prefer one deed over another? He said: Yes. I asked Ibn Mas'ud, and he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah and nearest? He said: Prayer at its time. I said: Then what next after that? He said: Then kindness to parents. I said: Then what next after that? He said: Striving in the path of Allah. Had I asked more, he would have given me more. I said: Which deeds are most hateful to Allah and furthest from Allah? He said: To set up a rival to Allah while He created you, to kill your child fearing he eat with you, and to commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. Then he recited: And those who do not call with Allah another god, nor kill the soul Allah forbade except by right, nor commit adultery; whoever does that meets punishment."
"9846","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Shaybah Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh: Ibn Mas'ud said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time. I said: Then which? He said: Kindness to parents. I said: Then which? He said: Striving in the path of Allah. By Allah, had I asked more, he would have given me more. I said: Which sin is greatest with Allah? He said: To set up a rival to Allah while He created you. I said: Then which? He said: To kill your child fearing he eat with you. I said: Then which? He said: To commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. We tarried but a little until Allah sent down its confirmation: And those who do not call with Allah another god, nor kill the soul Allah forbade except by right, nor commit adultery; whoever does that meets punishment. Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah rendered it well, while Hammad ibn Salamah did not render it well."
"9847","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Establishing prayer at its time. I said: Then what? He said: Then kindness to parents. I said: Then what? He said: Then striving in the path of Allah. Then he fell silent; had I asked more, he would have given me more. I said: Which sin is greatest? He said: To set up a rival for your Creator, to kill your child fearing he eat with you, and to commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. And the Quran came down: And those who do not call with Allah another god, nor kill the soul Allah forbade except by right, nor commit adultery; whoever does that meets punishment."
"9848","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deed is best? He said: Kindness to parents, and prayer at its time. Za'idah raised it, while Shu'bah and Hammad ibn Salamah stopped it."
"9849","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Asim, from Zirr: A man came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and said: Which ranks of Islam are best? He said: The prayers at their times."
"9850","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh: Ibn Mas'ud, having a lad with him, read the mushaf with his companions present, when a man called Khadramah came and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, which ranks of Islam are best? He said: Prayer. He said: Then which? He said: Almsgiving. He said: Then which? He said: Kindness to parents. He said: With whom is a man? He said: I think he said: With whom he loves."
"9851","A chapter. Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, adding or omitting in his prayer, Mansur said: It was Ibrahim who forgot that, from Alqamah, or Alqamah from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. Abdullah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and turned to us with his face, we said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new come in the prayer? He said: No. He was told what he had done; he folded his leg, faced the qiblah, prostrated twice, then turned away, saying: Had something new come in the prayer, I would have told you; but I am a human being like you, forgetting as you forget. When I forget, remind me. Whoever of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek what is likeliest correct, complete upon it, then salute and prostrate twice."
"9852","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer, adding or omitting therein. When he finished his prayer, we said: Has something been added in the prayer? He said: What is that? We said: You led us in such-and-such. He turned, folded his legs, prostrated twice, then turned to us with his face, saying: I am but a human being like you; when I forget, remind me. When any of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek the correct, complete it, then prostrate twice."
"9853","Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi' al-Naysaburi informed us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek what he deems correct, complete it, then prostrate twice."
"9854","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, adding or omitting. When he turned away, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new come in the prayer? He said: Had something come, I would have told you; I am but a human being, forgetting as you forget. Whoever of you prays, adding or omitting, let him seek the correct, complete it, and prostrate the two of forgetfulness."
"9855","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zanbur narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, adding or omitting, and he mentioned the like of it."
"9856","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' al-Misri narrated to us, Harun ibn Sa'id al-Ayli narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9857","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"9858","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he either added or omitted, Ibrahim said: By Allah, that came only from me. We said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new come in the prayer? He said: No. We told him what he had done. He said: When a man adds or omits, let him prostrate twice. He said: Then he prostrated twice."
"9859","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Durays narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hasin, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in the prescribed prayer, let him seek, then prostrate the two of forgetfulness."
"9860","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek the correct, and prostrate the two of forgetfulness while sitting."
"9861","9835 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Malik ibn Suayr narrated, Habib ibn Hassan narrated, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and he added or decreased, we said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in the prayer? He said: ""What is that?"" We said: You prayed such and such, so he faced the qiblah and prostrated two prostrations, then he gave salam."
"9862","9836 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in al-Asr prayer, then he stood up in the fourth without sitting, until he led us in a fifth, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you led us in five, so he faced the qiblah and said takbir and prostrated two prostrations."
"9863","9837 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Mindal narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim who said: Alqamah prayed al-Asr as five, so we said when he gave salam: You prayed five, so he said to a man from al-Nakha called Ibrahim ibn Suwayd: Is that so, O one-eyed? He said: Yes, so he led us in two prostrations while standing, then he recited tashahhud then gave salam, then he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in al-Asr as five, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer? He said: ""And what is that?"" We said: You prayed five, so he said to a man called Dhu al-Shimalayn: ""Is that so, O Dhu al-Yadayn?"" He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, so he led us in two prostrations while sitting, then he recited tashahhud then gave salam, then he said: O people, I am only a human like you, I forget as you forget, so when I forget then remind me, and when one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he added or decreased, let him seek what is correct, let him complete upon it and prostrate two prostrations; for if something had been added to your prayer I would have informed you."
"9864","9838 - al-Abbas ibn al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (H) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed al-Zuhr or al-Asr, and when he finished his prayer it was said: O Messenger of Allah, has a new matter happened in the prayer? He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: You prayed five, so he faced the qiblah and prostrated two prostrations then he said: I am only a human, I forget as you forget, so when one of you is mistaken in his prayer let him prostrate two prostrations."
"9865","9839 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, from Shubah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed al-Zuhr as five, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been increased? He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: You prayed five, so he prostrated two prostrations."
"9866","9840 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, Misar narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed five, so he prostrated two prostrations."
"9867","9841 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, both said: Shubah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed al-Zuhr as five rakahs, so they said to him: O Prophet of Allah, has the prayer been increased? So he gave salam then prostrated the two prostrations of error."
"9868","9842 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Shair narrated, Sahl ibn Hammad narrated, from Abu Bakr al-Nahshali, al-Haytham - meaning al-Sayrafi - narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"9869","9843 - Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah that he led the people in five rakahs, and when he finished they said: You prayed five rakahs, so Alqamah said: Is that what you say, O one-eyed? - meaning Ibrahim - He said: Yes, so Alqamah prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recited tashahhud and gave salam, then he turned to them and informed them from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he did that."
"9870","9844 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Hakim ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in five rakahs, and when he gave salam that was said to him, so he faced the qiblah and prostrated two prostrations, while sitting."
"9871","9845 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd who said: Alqamah led us in al-Zuhr as five, and when he finished they said to him: You prayed five, he said: I did not do it, then he said: Is that so, O one-eyed? He said: I said: Yes, so he turned and prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then gave salam, then he mentioned from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed five, so he saw them whispering to one another, so he said: ""What is the matter with you?"" So they said: Has the prayer been increased? He said: ""And what is that?"" They said: You prayed five, he said: No, but I forgot, so he turned and prostrated two prostrations."
"9872","9846 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi informed us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd who said: Alqamah led us as five, so it was said to him, so he said: I did not do it, so I said: Yes indeed, he said: And you, O one-eyed? I said: Yes, so he prostrated two prostrations, then he narrated to us from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed five, so the people whispered to one another and said: Has the prayer been increased? He said: ""No"", so they informed him, so he folded his leg and prostrated two prostrations then he said: I am a human, I forget as you forget."
"9873","9847 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shubah narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, that he prayed behind Alqamah ibn Qays, and he prayed five or six, so it was said to him: You were mistaken, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and he narrated from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he did the like of that."
"9874","9848 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed al-Zuhr or al-Asr as five, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two prostrations are for whoever among you thought he added or decreased."
"9875","9849 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us one day, then he mentioned the like of it."
"9876","9850 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated, Israil narrated, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"9877","9851 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, from Muhammad ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed al-Zuhr as five, so he prostrated two prostrations."
"9878","9852 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, both said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed five, and when he finished it was said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been increased? He said: ""No, and what is that?"" They said: You prayed five, he said: I am only a human like you, I remember as you remember, and I forget as you forget, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"9879","9853 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ishkab narrated, Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated, Abu Khalid al-Dalani narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in al-Zuhr or al-Asr as five, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been increased? He said: ""No, and what is that?"" They said: You prayed five, so he faced the qiblah and prostrated two prostrations, then he said: These two prostrations are for whoever among you thought he added or decreased."
"9880","9854 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer then he entered, so some of the people said to others: Has the prayer been increased? He said: ""And what is that?"" He said: You prayed five, so he took his hand, then he went out to the mosque, and there was a circle in which were Abu Bakr and Umar, so he said: Is what Dhu al-Yadayn says true? They said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah, so he faced the qiblah, then prostrated two prostrations."
"9881","Chapter. 9855 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid and Alqamah, from Abdullah, that a man came to him and said: I recited al-Mufassal in one rakah, so Abdullah said: Rather you rattled it off like the rattling off of poetry, and like the scattering of inferior dates, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite al-Nazair in one rakah, then he mentioned ten rakahs with twenty surahs according to the arrangement of Abdullah, the last of them: {When the sun is folded up}, and al-Dukhan."
"9882","9856 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, Sughdi ibn Sinan narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: Give every surah its share of bowing and prostration; for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not recite twenty surahs in ten rakahs."
"9883","9857 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated, Abdullah ibn Musa narrated, Isa ibn Qirtas narrated, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: A man came and said: I recited al-Mufassal in one rakah, so he said: Rattling off like the rattling off of poetry? Recite as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: two surahs of al-Mufassal in one rakah."
"9884","9858 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: I know the Nazair which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join together: two surahs in one rakah."
"9885","9859 - Ubayd al-Ijli - whose name is al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Tawil - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated, Harun ibn al-Ashath - and he was trustworthy - narrated, Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated, Shubah narrated, from Husayn - or Abu Husayn - from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: A man came and said: I recited al-Mufassal in one rakah, so he said: Rattling off like the rattling off of poetry? But the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite al-Nazair, two surahs, twenty surahs."
"9886","9860 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (H) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam informed us, both said: Hushaym narrated, Sayyar narrated, from Abu Wail who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: I recited al-Mufassal last night in one rakah, so he said: Scattering like the scattering of inferior dates, and rattling off like the rattling off of poetry? I know the Nazair which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join between: two surahs in one rakah, and the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Ubayd."
"9887","9861 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Azraq narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah who said: Abdullah said: I know the Nazair which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with: al-Dhariyat, al-Tur, Iqtarabat, al-Najm, al-Rahman, al-Waqiah, Nun, al-Haqqah, al-Muzzammil, La uqsimu bi-yawm al-qiyamah, Hal ata ala al-insan, al-Mursalat, Amma yatasaalun, al-Naziat, Abasa, Wayl lil-mutaffifin, Idha al-shamsu kuwwirat, and Ha-Mim al-Dukhan."
"9888","9862 - Salamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, the like of it."
"9889","9863 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah who said: I heard Abu Wail say: A man came to Abdullah and said: I recited al-Mufassal tonight in one rakah, so Abdullah said: Rattling off like the rattling off of poetry? I know the Nazair which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in one rakah, then he mentioned twenty surahs from the beginning of al-Mufassal, joining between two surahs."
"9890","9864 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: I know the Nazair which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in one rakah - then Abdullah stood, taking the hand of Alqamah, and Alqamah came out to us, so we said to him: Did he inform you of the Nazair? So he said: He said: The first twenty of al-Mufassal, among them a surah of Al-Hamim: al-Dukhan, its counterpart: {Amma yatasaalun}."
"9891","9865 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to me, Wasil al-Ahdab narrated, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: I remember the Qarain which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite: eighteen of al-Mufassal, and two surahs of Al-Hamim."
"9892","9866 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: I know the Nazair which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join between: two surahs in one rakah."
"9893","9867 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated, my father narrated, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Nuhayk ibn Sinan who said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said: I recited al-Mufassal in one rakah, so he said: Rattling off like the rattling off of poetry? I know the Nazair which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join: twenty surahs in ten rakahs."
"9894","9868 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Husayn, (H) and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to me, Ibn Abi Adi narrated, from Shubah, from Husayn, from Ibrahim, from Nuhayk ibn Sinan, from Abdullah ibn Masud, the like of it."
"9895","Chapter. 9869 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning a man who left his daughter and his son's daughter and his sister, so he gave the daughter half, and the son's daughter a sixth, and what remained to the sister."
"9896","9870 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"9897","9871 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi narrated to us, Adam narrated, Shubah narrated, (H) and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated, Shubah narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan informed me, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, that Abu Musa was asked about a daughter and a son's daughter and a sister, so he said: For the daughter is half, and for the sister is half, and he gave the son's daughter nothing, and he said: Ask Ibn Masud; for he will agree with me, so they asked Ibn Masud, and informed him of the saying of al-Ashari, so he said: I would have gone astray then and would not be of the guided, I judge between you with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""For the daughter is half, and for the son's daughter is a sixth, and for the sister is a third"", so it reached al-Ashari, so he said: Do not ask me about anything as long as this scholar is among you."
"9898","9872 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil who said: A man came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabiah concerning a daughter and a son's daughter and a full sister, so they said: For the daughter is half, and for the sister is half, and they did not give the son's daughter anything, and they said: Go to Abdullah ibn Masud; for he will agree with us, so the man came to him and asked him and informed him of their saying, so he said: I would have gone astray then and would not be of the guided, but I judge in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""For the daughter is half, and for the son's daughter a share completing two-thirds, and what remains is for the full sister."""
"9899","9873 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Muallim al-Dimashqi narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of the hadith of Ali ibn Mushir."
"9900","9874 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, that Abu Musa al-Ashari was asked about a man who left his daughter and his son's daughter and his full sister, so he said: For his daughter is half, and what remains is for the full sister, and he said to us: Ibn Masud will say the like of what I said, so they asked Ibn Masud, then they informed him of what Abu Musa said, he said: And how should I say the like of what he said? And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""For his daughter is half, and for the son's daughter is a sixth completing two-thirds, and what remains is for the full sister."""
"9901","9875 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Hamdani narrated, al-Rabi ibn Ziyad narrated, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil who said: A man came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabiah and asked them about a daughter and a son's daughter and a full sister, so they said: For the daughter is half, and for the sister is half, and they said: Abdullah ibn Masud will agree with us, so I came to Abdullah and mentioned their saying to him, so he said: I would have gone astray then and would not be of the guided, but I shall judge in it with what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged: ""For the daughter is half, and for the son's daughter is a sixth completing two-thirds, and what remains is for the sister."""
"9902","9876 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated, Ishaq ibn al-Azraq narrated, Misar narrated, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a daughter and a son's daughter and a sister: ""For the daughter is half, and for the son's daughter is a sixth, and what remains is for the sister."""
"9903","9877 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydah Abu Yusuf al-Madani narrated, al-Jarrah ibn Malih al-Bahrani narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla al-Qadi, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a daughter and a son's daughter and a sister: ""For the daughter is half, and for the son's daughter is a sixth, and what remains is for the sister."""
"9904","9878 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who tattoos and the woman who has herself tattooed, and the woman who joins hair and the woman who has hair joined to hers, and the eater of riba and the one who feeds it, and the muhallil and the one for whom muhallil marriage is done."
"9905","9879 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil who said: A man came to Ibn Masud and said to him: I had a slave and I freed him and made him a saibah in the path of Allah, so Abdullah said to him: The people of Islam do not make saibah, rather the people of Jahiliyyah used to make saibah, and you are his patron and the most entitled of people to his inheritance, so if you are uneasy about something then show it to us and we shall place it in the bayt al-mal."
"9906","9880 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Muawiyah narrated, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated, from Abu Malik al-Nakhai whose name is Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn, from Hajjaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join between al-Maghrib and al-Isha, delaying this one to the end of its time, and placing this one at the beginning of its time."
"9907","9881 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join between the two prayers while traveling."
"9908","9882 - Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ubaydah al-Tammar narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from his father - I think - from Layth - from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the most resembling of nations to the Children of Israil, you will surely follow their way step by step, until there is nothing among them except there will be the like of it among you, to the point that the people: a woman passes by them and one of them stands up to her and has intercourse with her, then he returns to his companions laughing to them and they laughing to him."
"9909","Chapter. 9883 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated, from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: I never heard anything better concerning tashahhud than the hadith of Ibn Masud; and that is that he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9910","9884 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Mihall ibn Muhriz al-Dabbi narrated who said: I heard Shaqiq ibn Salamah mention, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: They used to pray behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so one of them said: Peace be upon Allah, so he said: ""Who is the one who said: Peace be upon Allah? Allah, He is al-Salam, but say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."""
"9911","9885 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: Abu Nuaym narrated, al-Amash narrated, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: When we sat we used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard us and said: Allah, He is al-Salam, so when one of you sits in prayer let him say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah."
"9912","9886 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: When we sat in prayer we used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon us from our Lord, peace be upon Jibril and Mikail, peace be upon so-and-so, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, He is al-Salam, when you sit in prayer then say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, for when he says that it reaches every righteous servant in the heaven or on the earth, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, then let him choose of speech what he wishes."
"9913","9887 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Nuaym ibn Yahya al-Saidi narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"9914","9888 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad and Mansur and Husayn and al-Amash and Abu Hashim, from Abu Wail and Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: We did not know what to say in prayer, we used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mikail, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud and said: Allah, He is al-Salam, so when you sit in two rakahs then say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah - Abu Wail said in the hadith of Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When you say it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heaven and the earth, Abu Ishaq said in the hadith of Abdullah: When you say it, it reaches every angel brought near or messenger prophet or righteous servant - I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9915","9889 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya al-Kufi narrated, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"9916","9890 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam and Fudayl ibn Amr, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon Allah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and said: Do not say: Peace be upon Allah; for Allah, He is al-Salam, but say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9917","9891 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Sufyan ibn Uqbah al-Suwai narrated, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"9918","9892 - Ahmad ibn Ma Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Manjufi narrated, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from Hammad, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"9919","9893 - Ahmad ibn Rustah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated, al-Hakam ibn Ayyub narrated, from Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Masud who said: They used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon the Messenger of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say: Peace be upon Allah; for Allah, He is al-Salam, but say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9920","9894 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Asim ibn Bahdalah and Hammad informed us, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril and Mikail, and every angel whose name we know, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say: Peace be upon Allah; for Allah, He is al-Salam, then he taught us: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, so when you say this then every angel and every prophet and every righteous servant has entered into your saying."
"9921","9895 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammam narrated, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated, from Abu Wail who said: And Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to them and taught them the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9922","9896 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjulani informed us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon so-and-so, peace be upon so-and-so, naming whom we knew of the angels and the prophets, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Allah, He is al-Salam, then he taught us the tashahhud, and we used to learn it as one of us learns a surah of the Quran, he said: Say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9923","9897 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated, my father narrated to me, Said ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"9924","9898 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, or from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Masud who said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibrail, peace be upon Mikail, peace be upon the angels brought near, so the Prophet, upon him be peace, said: Do not say: Peace be upon Allah; Allah, He is al-Salam, he said: So he taught them the tashahhud and said: Say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9925","9899 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated, from Zaidah, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9926","9900 - Abu Mulayl Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi al-Kufi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Hirasa narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, and from Mihall, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9927","9901 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Wadih narrated to me, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from his father, and Mansur, and al-Amash, and Mughirah, and Hammad, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9928","9902 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Mughirah al-Dabbi narrated, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah who said: Abdullah said: We used to pray behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: Peace be upon Allah, so he said: Allah, He is al-Salam, but say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His Messenger."
"9929","9903 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Dahir ibn Nuh narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"9930","9904 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Mansur and Sulayman and Hammad and Abu Hashim and Mughirah, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Allah, He is al-Salam, but say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9931","9905 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated, Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated, Shubah narrated, from al-Hakam and Husayn, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"9932","9906 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Affan narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated, Hurayth narrated, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud and the khutbah as he taught us a surah of the Quran: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, to his saying: His servant and His Messenger."
"9933","9907 - al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Nasr al-Tusi narrated to us, Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated, Abu Sad narrated, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9934","9908 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hubab al-Himyari narrated, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated, Habib ibn Hassan narrated, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: When we sat we used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mikail, peace be upon the angels, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us words which when we say them we greet every angel in the heaven and every righteous servant on the earth: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9935","9909 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9936","9910 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew the openings of good and its comprehensive matters, or the comprehensive matters of good and its openings, and we did not know what to say in our prayer until he taught us, so he said: Say: Greetings, then he mentioned the like of it."
"9937","9911 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer as he taught us a surah of the Quran: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9938","9912 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Shubah narrated who said: Abu Ishaq informed us, Abu al-Ahwas informed us, from Abdullah who said: We did not know what to say in every rakah, we glorified and said takbir and praised our Lord, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taught the openings of good and its endings, or he said: its comprehensive matters, and he said to us: When you sit in every two rakahs then say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, and peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, then let him choose of supplication what pleases him most and supplicate with it."
"9939","9913 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, both said: Zuhayr narrated, (H) and Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated, al-Masudi narrated, H and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, (H) and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated, both said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated, from al-Amash, (H) and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Musa ibn Ayan narrated, from Hisham ibn Hassan, (H) and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad Nizak al-Tusi narrated, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, (H) and Ahmad ibn al-Khidr al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Marwazi narrated, Abu Muadh al-Nahwi narrated, Abu Hamzah narrated, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, (H) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated, (H) and al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from his father, (H) and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, Dawud ibn Abi Abdillah brother of Shaqiq narrated, (H) and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Zibaqi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated, from Ashath, from Sawwar, (H) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Sharik narrated, (H) and Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Zuhayr narrated, all of them from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud in prayer: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and the wording is that of the hadith of al-Amash from Abu Ishaq, and the others are similar to it."
"9940","9914 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim al-Qazzaz narrated, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, Abu al-Ahwas and al-Aswad ibn Yazid and Amr ibn Maymun and the companions of Abdullah informed me, that they heard him say: We did not know what to say in prayer, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: When you sit in every two rakahs then say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, then let him choose of supplication what pleases him most."
"9941","9915 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah and Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Quran: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9942","9916 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruwasi narrated, Musab ibn Mahan narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. Sufyan said: And Abu Muhammad narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah the like of it, Abu Muhammad is al-Amash."
"9943","9917 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Shafii al-Himsi narrated to us, Mirdad ibn Jamil narrated, Muhammad ibn Munadhir narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas and Abu al-Kanud, from Ibn Masud who said: We did not know what to say in every two rakahs of prayer except to say takbir and glorify and praise our Lord, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given the openings of good and its endings, he said: When you sit in tashahhud then say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9944","9918 - Salamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9945","9919 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ahmad al-Arzami narrated, my uncle narrated, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from one who heard Abu al-Ahwas say: I heard Abdullah say: I learned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Greetings, then he mentioned similar to it."
"9946","9920 - Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated, Ufayr ibn Madan narrated, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud and said: Say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9947","9921 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd al-Zari narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated, Ibn Awn narrated, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud: Say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9948","9922 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, Safadi ibn Sinan narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Quran and say: Learn; for there is no prayer except with tashahhud."
"9949","9923 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and taught me the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9950","9924 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, that he heard him say: Alqamah took my hand, and Abdullah ibn Masud took the hand of Alqamah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Ibn Masud and taught him the tashahhud in prayer: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9951","9925 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, (H) and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, they said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated, al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr al-Asadi narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah who said: Alqamah ibn Qays al-Nakhai took my hand and said: Abdullah ibn Masud took my hand and taught me the tashahhud, then he mentioned similar to it."
"9952","9926 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated, al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the hadith of Zuhayr."
"9953","9927 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated, from Talhah ibn Musarrif who said: Rabi ibn Khaytham added in the tashahhud: ""His blessings and His forgiveness"", so Alqamah said: We stop where we learned: ""Peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings."""
"9954","9928 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Nasr al-Jahdami narrated, Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated, Wuhayb narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9955","9929 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abidah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"9956","9930 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated, from Zaidah, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9957","9931 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah the like of it."
"9958","9932 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqashi narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite tashahhud in prayer, he said: And we used to memorize it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as we memorize the letters of the Quran, the waws and the alifs, he said: When he sat upon his left haunch he said: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, then he supplicates his God then gives salam and leaves."
"9959","9933 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ahmad al-Arzami narrated, my uncle narrated, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Abu Umamah, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, Abdullah ibn Masud narrated to me who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: When one of you sits in his prayer let him say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9960","9934 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah who said: We used to say in prayer: Peace be upon our Lord, so it was said to us: Say: Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, for when you say that you greet whoever is in the heaven and the earth."
"9961","9935 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Quran."
"9962","9936 - al-Husayn ibn Ulluwayh al-Qattan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Aishah narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, (H) and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated, Attab ibn Bashir narrated, both from Khusayf, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Quran: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9963","9937 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Burjani narrated, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mujahid narrated, Mujahid narrated to me who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla and Abu Mamar narrated to me, he said: Ibn Masud taught me the tashahhud, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, O Allah bless Muhammad and the people of his house as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, O Allah bless us along with them, O Allah bless Muhammad and the people of his house as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, O Allah bless us along with them, the blessings of Allah and the blessings of the believers upon Muhammad the unlettered Prophet, peace be upon him and the mercy of Allah and His blessings."
"9964","9938 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Anbasah, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught them the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"9965","9939 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated, from Hajjaj, from Umayr ibn Said, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Al-Ajlah raised it, and Hammad ibn Salamah did not raise it."
"9966","9940 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Umayr ibn Said who said: Ibn Masud taught me the tashahhud, then he mentioned the tashahhud then he said: O Allah I ask You of all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, O Allah I ask You of the best of what Your righteous servants asked You, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your righteous servants sought refuge, O Allah our Lord give us in this world good and in the Hereafter good, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."
"9967","9941 - Muhammad ibn al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Umayr ibn Said who said: I heard Abdullah say: When one of you sits in prayer let him say: Greetings, then he mentioned the tashahhud then he said: Let him say: O Allah I ask You of all good, what I knew of it and what I did not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I knew of it and what I did not know, O Allah I ask You the best of what Your righteous servants asked You of it, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your righteous servants sought refuge, Our Lord give us in this world good and in the Hereafter good and protect us from the punishment of the Fire, Our Lord we believed so forgive us our sins, and expiate from us our evil deeds, and cause us to die with the righteous, Our Lord and give us what You promised us upon Your messengers, and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You do not break the promise."
"9968","9942 - Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, Shayban narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir who said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud wrote to me: To proceed, I inform you of the guidance of Abdullah ibn Masud in prayer and his deed and his saying in it, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given the comprehensive words, he used to teach us how to say in prayer when we sit in it: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, then he asks what occurs to him after that, and desires of His mercy and His forgiveness, brief words with which he does not prolong the sitting, and he used to say: I love that your asking Allah when one of you sits in prayer and finishes the greeting be that he say after that: Glory be to You, there is no god other than You, forgive me my sin, and rectify for me my deed; indeed You forgive sins for whom You will, and You are the Forgiving, the Merciful, O Forgiver forgive me, O Accepter of repentance accept my repentance, O Merciful have mercy on me, O Pardoner pardon me, O Compassionate show compassion to me, O Lord inspire me to thank Your favor which You bestowed upon me, and gird me with excellent worship of You, O Lord I ask You of all good, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, O Lord open for me with good, and seal for me with good, and give me longing to meet You without harmful adversity, nor misguiding trial, and protect me from evil deeds, and whomever You protect from evil deeds then You have had mercy on him, and that is the great triumph. Then whatever of your supplication it is, let it be in humility and sincerity; for He loves the humility of His servant to Him.. Then Abdullah used to rise at midday when the sun rose, and pray four rakahs, and recite in them a surah of the Quran long and short, then he would remain only a little until he prayed al-Zuhr prayer, prolonging the standing in the first two rakahs, reciting in them two surahs: Alif-Lam-Mim, Tanzil, al-Sajdah, and the like of it of al-Mathani, so when he prayed al-Zuhr he bowed after it two rakahs, then he remained until when the sun declined and upon it was a long day he prayed al-Asr prayer, and recited in the first two rakahs two surahs of al-Mathani, or al-Mufassal, and they were shorter than what he recited in al-Zuhr prayer, so when he finished al-Asr prayer he did not pray after it until the sun set, so when he saw it had departed he prayed al-Maghrib prayer which you call al-Isha, and recited in them two surahs of the short al-Mufassal: {By the night when it covers} and {Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High}, and similar to them of the short al-Mufassal, then he bowed after it two rakahs, and he used to swear over it a swearing he did not swear over any of the prayers, by Allah besides whom there is no god that this hour is the appointed time of this prayer, and say: Its confirmation: {Establish the prayer from the decline of the sun to the darkness of the night and the Quran of dawn, indeed the Quran of dawn is witnessed}, and it is that which they call the Subh prayer, and at it the two guards gather, he held it dear to hear a speaker at that hour except with the remembrance of Allah and the recitation of the Quran, then he remained after until he prayed al-Isha, which you call al-Atamah, and recited in it the endings of Al Imran: {Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth}, to its end, and with the endings of Surah al-Furqan: {Blessed is He who made in the heaven constellations}, to its end, in measured recitation and beautiful voice with the Quran, and he used to say: A beautiful voice with the Quran is an adornment for it, so if he did not recite in it the endings of these two he recited the like of them of al-Mathani or al-Mufassal, so when he finished al-Isha prayer he bowed after it two rakahs, and he did not pray after any of the prescribed prayers except two rakahs. Then the Friday prayer, he used to pray after it four rakahs, until when it was the end of the night he stood and prayed witr what Allah decreed of prayer, either nine or seven, or above that, until when it was the time the dawn splits and he saw the horizon with darkness of the night upon it, he stood and prayed al-Subh, and recited in them two long surahs: al-Rad and the like of it of al-Mathani, until he would be suspected of letting the morning brighten, and he used to say takbir in everything of the prayer until he stands for it, and when he raised his head he would say: Allah hears him who praises Him, then he stands straight, then he praises his Lord and glorifies Him while standing, then he says takbir for the prostration until he falls prostrating, then he says takbir when he raises his head, then he sits straight and praises his Lord and glorifies Him, then he says takbir for the second prostration, then he says takbir when he raises his head from it, then he says takbir, then he stands from the sitting, so when he prayed his prayer he gave salam twice without turning or gesturing with his hand, then he attended to his need whether it was on his right or on his left, and when he stood for prayer he lowered his voice and his body in it, and the generality of his saying while standing was to glorify, and his glorification in it was: Glory be to You, there is no god but You, never ceasing from that."
"9969","The disagreement from al-Shabi in the hadith of Abdullah: that Muadh was an ummah obedient to Allah. 9943 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: It was recited in his presence - or he recited it - : {Indeed Ibrahim was an ummah obedient}, so Abdullah said: Muadh was an ummah obedient, they said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, {Indeed Ibrahim was an ummah obedient}, so Abdullah said: And do you know what al-Ummah is? The one who teaches people good, and al-Qanit: the one who obeys Allah and His Messenger."
"9970","9944 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, Firas informed me who said: I heard al-Shabi narrate from Masruq who said: Abdullah said: Muadh was an ummah obedient to Allah, upright, and was not of the polytheists, so Farwah - a man of Ashja - said: He forgot {Indeed Ibrahim}, so he said: And who forgot? We used to liken Muadh to Ibrahim, and he was asked about al-Ummah and said: Teacher of good, and he was asked about al-Qanit, so he said: Obedient to Allah and His Messenger."
"9971","9945 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Mujalid and Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: Muadh was an ummah obedient to Allah, upright, it was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, {Indeed Ibrahim was an ummah obedient to Allah, upright}, he said: He said: Did you hear me mention Ibrahim, then he said: Muadh was an ummah obedient to Allah, upright, he said: We used to liken Muadh to Ibrahim, peace of Allah be upon him."
"9972","9946 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, Shubah narrated, from Mujalid and Bayan, or one of them, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrate, from Masruq who said: Abdullah said: Muadh was an ummah obedient, so Farwah said: He erred, {Indeed Ibrahim was an ummah obedient}, so he said: We used to liken him to him, and he was asked about al-Ummah and said: Teacher of good, and he was asked about al-Qanit and said: Obedient to Allah and His Messenger."
"9973","9947 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, Ismail ibn Ullayah narrated, from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Shabi, Farwah ibn Nawfal al-Ashjai narrated to me who said: Ibn Masud said: Muadh was an ummah obedient to Allah, upright, so I said to myself: Abu Abd al-Rahman erred, rather He said: {Indeed Ibrahim}, he said: Do you know what al-Ummah is, and what al-Qanit is? He said: Allah knows best, he said: Al-Ummah is the one who teaches people good, and al-Qanit is the obedient to Allah and to His Messenger, and likewise was Muadh ibn Jabal teaching good, and obedient to Allah and to His Messenger."
"9974","9948 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, Dawud ibn Isa narrated, from al-Sari ibn Ismail, from al-Shabi, from Najiyah ibn Kab who said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: Muadh ibn Jabal was an ummah to Allah obedient, upright, and was not of the polytheists, so a man said: We do not see you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, narrating to us something you do not know what it is, Allah Almighty says: {Indeed Ibrahim}, and you say: Muadh, he said: They continue to hear from me truth and deny it, al-Qanit: the obedient to Allah, and Muadh was likewise."
"9975","9949 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from al-Shabi, from Abdullah the like of it, and he did not mention Masruq nor anyone else."
"9976","9950 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah: Muadh was an ummah obedient to Allah, do you know what al-Ummah is? He teaches people good."
"9977","The disagreement from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii in the hadith of Abdullah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Bring me three stones. 9951 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, so he ordered Ibn Masud to bring him three stones, so he came with two stones and dung, so he threw away the dung and said: This is filth, bring me a stone."
"9978","9952 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn, so he said to me: Seek for me three stones, so I found for him two stones and dung, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung and said: This is filth."
"9979","9953 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, they said: Zuhayr narrated, from Abu Ishaq who said: Abu Ubaydah is not the one he mentioned, but Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he wanted to relieve himself so he said: Bring me three stones, so I sought them and found two stones, and sought a third stone but did not find it, so I found dung and came with it, so he said: Did you not know that it is filth?"
"9980","9954 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the privy and said: Bring me three stones with which to clean myself, so I brought him two stones and dung, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung and said: It is filth."
"9981","9955 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to relieve himself, so he ordered me to bring him three stones, so I brought him two stones and dung, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung and said: This is filth."
"9982","9956 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Ibn Masud who said: I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered me to bring him three stones, so I brought him two stones and dung, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung, he said: It is filth."
"9983","9957 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me three stones, so he performed ablution without touching water, so I brought him two stones and dung, so he said: Throw away the dung; for it is filth."
"9984","9958 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself and said: Bring me something with which to clean myself, and do not bring me a bone nor dung, so I did, then he performed ablution and prayed."
"9985","9959 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjulani narrated, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself and said: Bring me something, and do not bring me a bone nor dung, so I did, so he performed ablution then prayed."
"9986","9960 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated, Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me three stones, so I brought him two stones and the dung of a donkey, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung and said: It is impurity."
"9987","The chains of the hadith of Abdullah ibn Masud on the night of the jinn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Chapter of whoever mentioned from Abdullah ibn Masud that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn. 9961 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated, Qays ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from Hanash, from Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Masud, that he performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with nabidh, so he performed ablution and said: A pure drink."
"9988","9962 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Fazarah al-Abdi, from Abu Zayd freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, Abdullah ibn Masud narrated who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: I have been commanded to recite to your brothers of the jinn, so let a man of you stand with me, and let no man stand in whose heart is a grain's weight of pride, so I stood with him, and I took a water-skin in which was nabidh, and I went with him, and when he emerged he drew a line for me and said to me: Do not leave it; for if you leave it you will not see me nor I see you until the Day of Resurrection, he said: Then he went and disappeared from me until I did not see him, and when dawn broke he came and said to me: Do I see you standing? So I said: I did not sit, so he said: What would be upon you if you did? I said: I feared to leave it, so he said: Had you left it you would not have seen me nor I seen you until the Day of Resurrection, is with you ablution water? I said: No, so he said: What is this water-skin? I said: In it is nabidh, he said: A good date, and pure water, so he performed ablution and established the prayer, and when he finished the prayer two men of the jinn stood to him and asked him for provision, so he said: Did I not order for you and for your people what benefits you? They said: Yes, but we loved that some of us witness the prayer with you, he said: From whom are you? They said: From the people of Nasibin, so he said: These two have succeeded, and their people have succeeded, and he assigned to them dung and bones as food and meat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cleaning oneself with a bone or dung."
"9989","9963 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri and Israil, from Abu Fazarah al-Abdi, Abu Zayd freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth narrated, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: When it was the night of the jinn two men of them stayed behind, saying: We shall witness Fajr with you O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is with you water? I said: There is no water with me, but with me is a water-skin in which is nabidh, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good date and pure water, so he performed ablution, Israil said in his hadith: Then he prayed al-Subh."
"9990","9964 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the night of the jinn: What is in your water-skin? He said: Nabidh, he said: A good date, and pure water."
"9991","9965 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Imran ibn Musa al-Qazzaz narrated, Abd al-Warith Abu Abdillah al-Shaqari narrated, from Sharik, from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought ablution water on the night of the jinn, so I said: There is nothing with me except nabidh in a water-skin, so he said: A good date, and pure water, so he performed ablution from it."
"9992","9966 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, my father narrated to me, (H) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, my uncle narrated, my father narrated, Abu Umays Utbah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated to me, from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was among a group of his companions, when he said: Let a man of you stand with me, and let no man stand with me in whose heart is a grain of deceit, so I stood with him and took the water-skin, and I do not think it was but water, and I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when he was at the heights of Makkah I saw black figures gathered, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a line for me, then he said: Stand here until I come to you, so I stood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to them, and I saw them crowding to him, he said: So the Messenger spent a long night, until he came to me with dawn, so he said: Have you remained standing O Ibn Masud after? So I said to him: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), did you not say to me: Stand until I come to you? Then he said to me: Is with you any ablution water? I said: Yes, so I opened the water-skin, and it was nabidh, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I took it and thought it was but water, and it is nabidh, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good date, and pure water, then he performed ablution from it, and when he stood to pray two persons of them came, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we love that you lead us in our prayer, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arranged them behind him, then he prayed with us, and when he finished I said to him: Who are these O Messenger of Allah? He said: These are the jinn of Nasibin, and they asked me for provision, so I provided them with dung and bones, whatever dung they find they find it barley, and whatever bone they find they find it clothed with meat, so at that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cleaning oneself with dung and with bone."
"9993","9967 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, Waki narrated, my father narrated from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd, freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the night of the jinn: Is with you purification? He said: No, except nabidh in a water-skin, so he said: A good date, and pure water, so he performed ablution."
"9994","9968 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Dahir ibn Nuh narrated, Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, from Musa, from Ubaydah, Said ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abu al-Mualla, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out before the Hijrah to the outskirts of Makkah, so he drew a line for me, and said: Do not do anything until I come to you, then he said: Let nothing you see frighten you, nor alarm you, he said: So he advanced a little then sat, and there were black men as if they were men of al-Zutt, he said: And they were as Allah Almighty said: {They almost crowded upon him}, so I wanted to stand and defend him as far as I could, then I remembered the covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I remained, then they dispersed from him, and I heard them say: O Messenger of Allah, our land is far and we are departing, so provide us, so he said: For you is dung, and whatever bone you come upon then for you upon it is meat, and whatever dung you come upon then it is for you dates, so when they turned I said: Who are these? He said: These are the jinn of Nasibin."
"9995","9969 - Muhammad Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi Burdah al-Bajali al-Dhahabi narrated, Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami narrated, from Harb ibn Subayh, Said ibn Muslim narrated, from Abu Murrah al-Sanani, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me with him on the night of the jinn, so I went with him until we reached the heights of Makkah, so he drew a line for me, and said: Do not move, then he went into the mountains, and I saw men coming down upon him from the tops of the mountains until they came between me and him, so I drew the sword and said: I shall strike until I rescue the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I remembered his saying: Do not move until I come to you, he said: So I remained thus until dawn secured us, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while I was standing, so he said: Have you remained in your state? I said: Had you remained a month I would not have moved until you come to me, then I informed him of what I intended to do, so he said: Had you left, I and you would not have met until the Day of Resurrection, then he interlaced his fingers in my fingers, and said: I was promised that the jinn and mankind would believe in me, as for mankind they have believed in me, and as for the jinn you have seen, he said: And I do not think my term but has drawn near, I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Abu Bakr as successor? So he turned away from me, so I saw that he did not agree with him, I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Umar as successor? So he turned away from me, so I saw that he did not agree with him, I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Ali as successor? He said: That, by the One besides whom there is no god, if you pledge allegiance to him and obey him He will admit you to Paradise all together."
"9996","9970 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, from his father, from Mina, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the delegation of the jinn, so he breathed, so I said: What is the matter with you O Messenger of Allah? He said: My death has been announced to me O Ibn Masud, I said: Appoint a successor, he said: Whom? I said: Abu Bakr, he said: So he was silent, then a while passed then he breathed, so I said: What is your matter, may my father and mother be ransom for you O Messenger of Allah? He said: My death has been announced to me O Ibn Masud, I said: Then appoint a successor, he said: Whom? I said: Umar, so he was silent, then a while passed then he breathed, so I said: What is your matter? He said: My death has been announced to me O Ibn Masud, I said: Then appoint a successor, he said: Whom? I said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they obey him they will all enter Paradise all together."
"9997","Chapter of whoever narrated from Ibn Masud that he was not with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn. 9971 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: I was not with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn, and I wished I had been with him."
"9998","9972 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, both said: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Abu Hamzah narrated, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took off his sandals while praying, so those behind him took off their sandals, so he said: What carried you to take off your sandals? They said: We saw you take off so we took off, so he said: Jibril, peace of Allah be upon him, informed me that in one of them was filth, so I took them off for that, so do not take off your sandals."
"9999","9973 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated, Abu Hamzah narrated, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform qunut except for a month, he did not perform qunut before it nor after it."
"10000","9974 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Nusayr who is Ibn Abi al-Ashath, from Maymun who is Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for thirty days supplicating, then he left it."
"10001","9975 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith narrated, from his father, from Bakr ibn Wail, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his houses were on his left, so when he prayed the prayer he went to his houses on his left."
"10002","9976 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq and he rode it, he and Jibril, peace of Allah be upon them both, so it carried them, and when it came upon a mountain its legs rose, and when it descended its hands rose, until he came to a gloomy foul land, then to a spacious pleasant land, I said: O Jibril, we were traveling in a gloomy foul land, then to a spacious pleasant land, so he said: That is the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise, he said: So I came upon a man while he was standing praying, so he said: Who is this with you O Jibril? I said: Your brother Muhammad, so he welcomed and supplicated for blessing, he said: Ask for ease for your ummah, he said: Who is this O Jibril? He said: Your brother Musa, I said: Upon whom was his voice and his complaint to his Lord? He said: Yes, he knows that of him and his severity, he said: Then we traveled and I saw lamps and light, so I said: Who is this O Jibril? He said: This is the tree of your father Ibrahim, I said: Shall I approach it? He said: Yes, so we approached it, so he supplicated for me for blessing and welcomed me, then we went to Bayt al-Maqdis, so I tied the beast with the ring with which the prophets tie, then I entered the mosque, and the prophets were spread out for me, whom Allah named in His Book and whom He did not name, so I prayed with them except the first of al-Baqar: Isa and Musa and Ibrahim, peace of Allah be upon them."
"10003","9977 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Abu Malik al-Nakhai informed us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had hardship been in a hole, ease would enter upon it until it brings it out, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {Indeed with hardship is ease}."
"10004","9978 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan al-Marrudhi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: Wailing is of the affair of Jahiliyyah."
"10005","9979 - al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated, (H) and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated, Abd al-Warith narrated, both from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: I used to see the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he gave salam to his right and to his left."
"10006","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Hamza, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: We were only commanded to fast Ashura before Ramadan was revealed; when Ramadan was revealed we were neither commanded it nor forbidden it."
"10007","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hamza, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to order Bilal to establish the prayer, then turn to people who hear the call and do not answer and burn their houses over them."
"10008","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Abu Hamza, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: Whoever dislikes wiping (over the footgear) has disliked the Sunna of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10009","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Abu Hamza, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: No concession was given to leave the congregation except to one fearful or sick."
"10010","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when al-Hasan and al-Husayn passed by as two boys, and he said: Bring me my two sons that I may seek refuge for them as Ibrahim sought refuge for his two sons Ismail and Ishaq. He said: I seek refuge for you two in the perfect words of Allah from every harmful eye, and from every devil and vermin."
"10011","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's paternal uncle is like his father. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) collected from al-Abbas two years' charity in one year."
"10012","Muhammad ibn Abda al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Tawba al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sharik, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no forgetfulness (prostration of sahw) in the fear prayer."
"10013","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the two sellers differ over the sale, they cancel the sale."
"10014","Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Isbahani and Abdullah ibn Bundar al-Isbahani narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: We used to eat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we heard the food glorifying Allah."
"10015","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Baraka ibn Muhammad al-Halabi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Asbat narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama who said: I came to Ibn Masud on the day of Ashura, and before him was a bowl of tharid and meat; I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, is this not the day of Ashura? He said: Yes; we used to fast it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before the month of Ramadan was made obligatory, and when the month of Ramadan was made obligatory it abrogated it. Then he said: Sit down; so I sat and ate."
"10016","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizma narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Hamza narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey two rak'as, and with Abu Bakr and Umar."
"10017","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar we faced him."
"10018","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Muallal ibn Nufayl al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Mihsan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to be named Harith, or Walid, or Hakam, or Abu al-Hakam, or Aflah, or Najih, or Yasar, and said: The most beloved names to Allah Almighty are those expressing servitude to Him."
"10019","Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Sijistani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking the lawful is an obligation after the (prescribed) obligation."
"10020","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only performed qunut for thirty nights, supplicating against tribes of Banu Sulaym and Ril and Dhakwan and Usayya, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"10021","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep in his prostration, and his sleep was known only by his snoring; then he would rise in his prayer."
"10022","Al-Hasan ibn Hubash al-Himmani al-Kufi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10023","Al-Hasan ibn Hubash al-Himmani narrated to us, Ali ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Musa ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ibn Masud who said: I saw the moon split in two, with Hira between them."
"10024","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us that when one of us sneezes we say tashmit to him (may Allah have mercy on you)."
"10025","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: Tell us when would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform witr? He said: When there remained of the night about as much as had passed of it by the Maghrib prayer; then they asked him about his recitation, and he said: He used to let the people of the house hear."
"10026","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs al-Qasmali narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim al-Qasmali narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance, and none shall enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith."
"10027","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus and Ibn al-Isbahani narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10028","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Ahwal narrated to us, Abu Ubayda ibn Man narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And whoever does that shall meet punishment."
"10029","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Masud: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deliver the sermon standing or sitting? He said: Do you not read: And they left you standing?"
"10030","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: Sad on the day of Badr fought the fighting of the horseman and the foot soldier."
"10031","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: Whoever goes to a fortune-teller or a soothsayer believing what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10032","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Budayl al-Yami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Looking at the face of Ali is worship."
"10033","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubayda al-Askari narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Talib al-Bazzaz narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn al-Shaddakh narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever spends generously on his family on the day of Ashura will remain in plenty the rest of his year."
"10034","Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ubayda ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Hammad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has close companions among his Companions, and my close ones among my Companions are Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"10035","Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sadan ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the moon split; one part went behind the mountain, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness, bear witness."
"10036","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Talha al-Yarbui narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not cleanse yourselves with dung or bones, for it is the provision of your brothers among the jinn."
"10037","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: When the prohibition of wine was revealed, the Jews said: Were not your brothers who died used to drink it? Then Allah Almighty revealed: There is no sin upon those who believe and do righteous deeds in what they tasted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And it was said to me: You are one of them."
"10038","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: I read to Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari, al-Abbas ibn al-Haytham al-Antaki narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us istikhara and said: When one of you intends a matter let him say: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek power from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty; for You know and I do not know, and You decree and I do not decree, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If that which I intend is good for my religion and the end of my affair, make it easy for me; and if other than that is better for me, decree good for me wherever it is. He says that, then he resolves."
"10039","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama who said: I went with Abdullah ibn Masud on Friday and found three who had preceded him, and he said: The fourth of four, and the fourth of four is not far from Allah; I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: People will sit from Allah on the Day of Resurrection according to their early going to the Fridays, the first, then the second, then the third, then the fourth. Then he said: The fourth of four, and the fourth of four is not far from Allah."
"10040","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The closest a servant is to Allah is when he is prostrating."
"10041","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqa al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Anbasa al-Warraq narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Mutayyab al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer comes out with sweat, and the soul of the disbeliever flows out as the soul of the donkey comes out; the believer does a sin and is made severe upon at death to expiate it, and the disbeliever does a good deed and is made easy upon at death to be recompensed for it."
"10042","Salama ibn Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Khaybar; he wanted to relieve himself, and when he wanted that he went far so no one would see him. He said: Look, O Abdullah, do you see anything? I looked and saw one tree, and told him. He said to me: Look, do you see anything? I looked and saw another tree far from its companion, and told him. He said: Tell them both: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to come together. I told them that and they came together; then he came to them and screened himself with them, then he stood and each one went back to its place. Then severe thirst struck the people in that expedition, and he said to me: O Abdullah, seek water for me. I brought him leftover water I found in a waterskin; he took it and poured it into a small vessel, then placed his hand in it and mentioned the name (of Allah). The water began to flow from between his fingers; the people drank and performed ablution as much as Allah willed. Abdullah said: I said: It is blessing; so I drank from it much, seeking its blessing. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned toward Madina, and a camel whose eyes had shed tears met him. He said: Whose camel is this? They said: Of Banu so-and-so. He said: It has sought refuge with me. They said: They intended to slaughter it; it worked for them until it grew old and weak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not slaughter it, and treat it well."
"10043","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and Alqama, from Ibn Masud who said: The two sons of Mulayka came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, our mother used to honor her husband and be kind to her child, and he mentioned the guest, except that she buried (a daughter) alive in the Jahiliyya. He said: Your mother is in the Fire. They turned away with evil seen in their faces; he ordered them and they were brought back with joy seen in their faces, hoping something had happened. He said: My mother is with your mother. A man of the hypocrites said: What avails this for his mother, while we tread on his heel? A man of the Ansar said, and I never saw a man who asked more than him: O Messenger of Allah, has your Lord promised anything concerning her or them? He said: Do you think it is of anything? He said: I have not asked my Lord, and I shall stand the Praised Station on the Day of Resurrection. The Ansari said: What is that Praised Station? He said: That is when you are brought barefoot unclothed; the first to be clothed will be Ibrahim (peace be upon him); He says: Clothe My intimate friend; he is brought two white garments and wears them, then he sits facing the Throne; then I am brought my clothing and wear it, and I stand at his right a station none other than I shall stand, envied by the first and the last for it; and my river Kawthar is opened to the Pond. A man of the hypocrites said: Water never flows except over pebbles or gravel. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what pebbles and gravel? He said: Its pebbles are musk and its gravel is camphor. The hypocrite said: I never heard like today; water that flows over pebbles or gravel must have plants. The Ansari said: O Messenger of Allah, does it have plants? He said: Yes, rods of gold. The hypocrite said: I never heard like today; no rod grows without leaves and fruit. The Ansari said: Does it have fruit? He said: Yes, varieties of jewels; its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst, and whoever is deprived of it will never be quenched after. And al-Saqu ibn Hazn narrated this hadith from Ali ibn al-Hakam, differing with Said ibn Zayd in its chain."
"10044","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, al-Saqu ibn Hazn narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The two sons of Mulayka came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the same."
"10045","Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himaya, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: You and your wealth belong to your father."
"10046","Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marrudhi and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Qadi al-Himsi narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined (his fingers/hands in prayer, tabbaqa)."
"10047","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Salih ibn Malik al-Khuwarizmi narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: We never fasted twenty-nine with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than we fasted thirty."
"10048","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari and Abu Aqil Anas ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to us, they said: al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Unaysa, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama and al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud who said: There were acts the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do and the people left them; one of them is the taslim of the imam in the funeral prayer like his taslim in the (prescribed) prayer."
"10049","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, Said ibn Zarbi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Alqama ibn Qays who said: I was a man to whom Allah had given a beautiful voice with the Quran; Ibn Masud used to send for me and I recited the Quran to him; when I finished my recitation he said: Give us more of this, may my father and mother be ransom for you; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A beautiful voice is the adornment of the Quran."
"10050","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Saffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Uththam ibn Ali ibn Said ibn al-Khims narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about whispering (waswasa), and said: That is pure faith."
"10051","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, from Qays, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed part of eloquence is magic."
"10052","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar and Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, they said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Hafs ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The cow is for seven, and the camel is for seven in the sacrifices."
"10053","Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Baghdadi and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Attar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of young men, upon you is marriage; for it is more guarding for the private part and more lowering for the gaze; whoever cannot do that, upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him."
"10054","Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Said al-Missisi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Maysara ibn Abd Rabbihi, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me to wake on my fast day oiled and combed, and not to wake on your fast day frowning; answer the invitation of whoever invites you among the Muslims so long as they do not openly show instruments of music; if they openly show instruments do not answer them; pray over whoever dies of our qibla, even if killed crucified or stoned; for meeting Allah with sins like the earth-full is better for you than withholding testimony from anyone of the people of the qibla."
"10055","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Hafs ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he raised it (to the Prophet): Do you know which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The best charity is granting: that one grants a dirham, or the back of a riding animal."
"10056","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Mamar ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty loves that His concessions be accepted as He loves that His strict obligations be fulfilled."
"10057","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dahir al-Razi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama and al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a group of Banu Hashim came; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them his face reddened and his eyes filled with tears. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we continually see in your face something we dislike? He said: We are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over this world, and my household will meet after me trial and expulsion."
"10058","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to me, Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say takbir at every rising and lowering, and greet to his right and to his left, until the whiteness of his face was seen from both sides."
"10059","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Kab narrated to us, Musa ibn Umayr narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All creation are the dependents of Allah; the most beloved of creation to Allah is the most beneficial of them to His dependents."
"10060","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Amr ibn Abdillah al-Awdi narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhill, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loses a child, male or female, whether it uttered (the testimony) or not, whether he is content or not, has no reward but Paradise."
"10061","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Asadi narrated to us, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10062","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Yazid ibn al-Walid, from Ibrahim, from Alqama who said: Abdullah stood upon al-Safa at a cleft in it and said: Here, by the One besides whom there is no god, stood the one to whom Surat al-Baqara was revealed."
"10063","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bazigh narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Umara, from al-Hakam, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a sheep whose milk was withheld, if he is pleased with it (he keeps it), otherwise he returns it with a sa of dates."
"10064","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bazigh narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Umara, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the (incoming) produce (to buy before it reaches the market)."
"10065","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bazigh narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Umara, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The (injury by a) dumb beast and the mine are without liability, and the grazing animal is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"10066","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when an uncovered woman came; that distressed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he closed his eyes. A man of the people stood to her, cast a garment over her and drew her to himself. One of his companions said: O Messenger of Allah, I think she is his wife. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do I consider her other than jealous? Allah Almighty has written jealousy upon women and jihad upon men; whoever of them is patient in faith and seeking reward shall have like the reward of the martyrs."
"10067","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Let those of you with understanding and intellect stand nearest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them; do not differ, lest your hearts differ; and beware the clamors of the markets."
"10068","Yahya ibn Muadh al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Sadusi narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes twist the forelock of his horse with his hand."
"10069","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Mughira said to me: I heard something from Umara ibn al-Qaqa which he mentioned from Ibrahim, and Umara had gone out to Makka, so I hired a donkey and came to him at al-Qadisiyya, and he narrated to me from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be passed by young men of his household and his color would change for that. One day young men of his household passed him and his color changed for that. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we continually see from you what distresses us; young men of your household pass you and your color changes for that. He said: These my household, Allah has chosen for them the Hereafter and has not chosen for them this world."
"10070","Al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Muadh, from Abd al-Karim, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no retaliation except with the sword."
"10071","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from Urfuta, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: Five verses have passed, and five of them remain: the splitting of the moon, and we saw it; the Smoke has passed, the Great Assault has passed, the Barren Day has passed, and the Binding has passed."
"10072","Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Farwa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Harun, that Sinan ibn al-Harith narrated to him, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Nakhai, from Alqama ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My description is Ahmad the trusting; not harsh nor rude; he repays good with good, and does not requite evil; his birthplace is Makka, his emigration place is Tayba, his nation are the much-praising; they gird at their middles and wash their extremities; their Gospels are in their chests; they line for prayer as they line for battle; their offering by which they draw near to Me is their blood; monks by night, lions by day."
"10073","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Musa narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, Ibrahim al-Nakhai narrated to us, from Alqama, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every good deed is charity, whether to rich or poor."
"10074","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khalifa ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Farqad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You are not ascetic until you are humble."
"10075","Muhammad ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The soul of the believer comes out with sweat, and I do not like a death like the death of the donkey. It was said: What is the death of the donkey? He said: The soul of the disbeliever comes out of his jaws."
"10076","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Bara narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Bakr ibn Khunays, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: A ruqya for fever was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Show it to me. They showed it to him: In the name of Allah, a piercing wound, a horn, salt, sea, qafta. He said: These are covenants Sulayman ibn Dawud, peace be upon him, took over pests, and I see no harm in it."
"10077","Abdullah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Madaini narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bazi al-Khaffaf al-Raqqi narrated to us, Said ibn Maslama narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting three days: hastening a day before Tarwiya, and (the day of) Fitr, and (the day of) Adha."
"10078","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he sought choice (istikhara) in a matter he intended to do he would say: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek power from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty; for You decree and I do not decree, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this is good for me in my religion, and good for me in my livelihood, and good for me in what I seek good thereby, choose for me in well-being, make it easy, then bless me in it; and if other than that is better for me, decree good for me wherever it is."
"10079","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us,Aidh ibn Habib narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Rabia narrated to us, Yazid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fighting the oath-breakers, the unjust, and the renegades."
"10080","Al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Duri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Harithi, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: Ali commanded fighting the oath-breakers, the unjust, and the renegades."
"10081","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Sulami narrated to us, Isa ibn Qirtas narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, and Mudar is at the tails of camels."
"10082","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Isa al-Hannat informed me, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is cursed, its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the eater of its price."
"10083","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Isa ibn Abi Isa informed me, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed usury, its eater and its giver, its scribe and its witness, while they know, and the woman who lengthens hair (with extensions) and the one for whom it is done, the tattooed and the tattooing, the plucker and the plucked, and forbade wailing."
"10084","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Sulami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then the second, then the third, then there will come a people with no good in them."
"10085","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, and Abdan ibn Ahmad and Shuayb ibn Imran al-Askari narrated to us, they said: Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman who buries (her daughter) alive and the buried girl are in the Fire."
"10086","Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Dawud al-Awdi, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: Whoever is pleased to read the page of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon which is his seal, let him read: Say: Come, I will recite what your Lord has forbidden to you, up to His saying: That you may be God-fearing."
"10087","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Dawud al-Awdi, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Abdullah, concerning His saying: O you who believe, do not consume your wealth among you unjustly except it be trade by mutual consent, he said: It is decisive, not abrogated."
"10088","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada narrating, from a companion of his, from Alqama ibn Qays, from Abdullah who said: While we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we heard a caller calling: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the fitra. Then he said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah; he said: He has come out thereby from the Fire. We hastened and found a shepherd with his sheep; the prayer time had come and he called it."
"10089","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu Zayd al-Nahwi narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his journeys he heard a caller saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the fitra. He said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has come out of the Fire."
"10090","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Alqama ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like."
"10091","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Habib ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: When Ibrahim son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, the sun eclipsed; the people said: It eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim son of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon them both. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life; when you see that, pray until it clears."
"10092","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sadan ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None shall enter Paradise with the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance, and none shall enter the Fire with the weight of a mustard seed of faith."
"10093","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Nubata al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: I read the Quran to Talha ibn Sulayman brother of Ishaq ibn Sulayman, and Talha said to me: I read to al-Fayyad ibn Ghazwan, and al-Fayyad said: I read to Talha ibn Musarrif al-Yami, and Talha said: I read to Yahya ibn Waththab, and Yahya ibn Waththab read to Alqama ibn Qays, and Alqama ibn Qays read to Abdullah ibn Masud, and Abdullah ibn Masud read to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Master of the Day of Judgment, with alif, lowering (the case of) Other than those angered upon."
"10094","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Makhlad Abu Khidash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Alqama and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, that he read: You shall surely ride stage upon stage, he said: O Muhammad, you shall surely ride heaven after heaven."
"10095","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This dinar and dirham destroyed those before you, and I see them only destroying you."
"10096","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Makhlad al-Basri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I said to al-Amash: From whom did you read: And the defilement, shun? He said: I read to Yahya ibn Waththab, and Yahya read to Alqama, and Alqama read to Abdullah, and Abdullah read to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10097","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When people differ, Ibn Sumayya is with the truth."
"10098","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same, and he did not mention Alqama."
"10099","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, and from Umara, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You will see after me favoritism and matters you disapprove of. We said: What do you command us? He said: Give them their right, and ask Allah for your right."
"10100","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Yaish narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Abi Ammar, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"10101","Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Isbahani narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ubayda al-Tammar narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man will come holding the hand of a man and say: O Lord, this one killed me. Allah Almighty will say: Why did you kill him? He will say: That might be Yours. He will say: It is Mine. He said: And a man will come holding the hand of a man and say: O Lord, this one killed me. Allah will say: Why did you kill him? He will say: I killed him that might be for so-and-so. He will say: It is not his; bear his sin."
"10102","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi al-Misri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from Zubayd al-Yami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis al-Nakhai, from a man described with a description thought to be Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that people of Kufa came to him; he greeted them with peace, commanded them to fear Allah, and not to differ over the Quran nor dispute in it; for it does not differ, nor fall apart, nor wear out with much repetition. Do you not see that the law of Islam in it is one, its limits, its recitation, and Allah's command in it? Had one of the two readings commanded something the other forbade, that would be disagreement; but it gathers all that. I hope there has come among you of understanding and knowledge among the best in people; had I known one reachable by camels more knowledgeable of what Allah revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than I, I would have sought him, until I added his knowledge to my knowledge. I knew that the Quran was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every year once, and it was presented to him twice in the year he died. When I recited the Quran to him he told me I do well; whoever reads upon my reading, let him not leave it turning from it; for whoever denies a letter of it denies all of it."
"10103","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, reaching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The fasting person has two joys: joy at his breaking, and joy when he meets his Lord; and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10104","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Masud, raising it: Allah Almighty said: Fasting is Mine, and I reward for it; the fasting person has two joys: joy when he breaks, and joy when he meets his Lord; and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10105","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, they said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud in need: Praise belongs to Allah, we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls; whom Allah guides none misguides, and whom He misguides none guides; and I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"10106","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubayda who said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the sermon of need: Praise belongs to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help; whom Allah guides none misguides, and whom He misguides none guides; and I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; O you who believe, fear Allah and speak upright words, the verse; O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims; O people, fear your Lord who created you, to the end of the verse; as to what follows."
"10107","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began strange, so glad tidings to the strangers."
"10108","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer is heavier upon the hypocrites than the Isha and Fajr prayers; had they known the merit in them they would have come to them even crawling."
"10109","Ubayd al-Ijli and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man will be bridled by sweat on the Day of Resurrection and say: Lord, relieve me even to the Fire."
"10110","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurara narrated to us, Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept he placed his right hand under his right cheek and said: Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants."
"10111","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Arara narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyash ibn Amr al-Amiri narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to me, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to read in Fajr on Friday the revelation of al-Sajda, and Has there come upon man."
"10112","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There was a man praying; when he prostrated a man came and stepped on his neck. The one beneath said: By Allah, He will never forgive him. Allah Almighty said: My servant swore upon Me that I would not forgive My servant; I have forgiven him."
"10113","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Muafa al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two fasts, two prayers, two garments, two foods, two marriages, and two sales: as for the two days, the day of Fitr and the day of Adha; as for the two prayers, prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and prayer after Asr until the sun sets; as for the two garments, to wrap in one garment with nothing between his private part and the sky, called al-samma; as for the two foods, to eat with his left while his right is sound, and to eat reclining; as for the two sales, a man saying: Sell for me and I sell for you; as for the two marriages, marriage of the prostitute, and marriage over the maternal and paternal aunt."
"10114","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ruzzi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Waqid al-Saffar narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah of His bounty; for Allah Almighty loves to be asked, and the best worship is awaiting relief."
"10115","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."
"10116","Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari al-Qadi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters."
"10117","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that Abu Bakr asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What has made you gray, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Hud and al-Waqia."
"10118","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a man stood, and a man after him spoke ill of him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clean your teeth. He said: With what shall I clean, O Messenger of Allah, I ate no meat? He said: You ate the flesh of your brother."
"10119","Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Sami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Ghassan narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four."
"10120","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed part of eloquence is magic."
"10121","Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Isbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Sharik and Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: We were commanded to establish prayer and give zakat; whoever does not give zakat has no prayer."
"10122","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubayda ibn Man narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these words: O Allah, I ask You guidance and piety, chastity and sufficiency."
"10123","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."
"10124","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds by twenty-five prayers, each like his prayer at home."
"10125","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to me, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Muwarriq al-Ijli, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-five prayers."
"10126","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Uqba ibn Wassaj, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10127","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu Zayd al-Nahwi Said ibn Aws narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"10128","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifa ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees."
"10129","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds a man's prayer alone by some twenty prayers."
"10130","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Salt narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to me, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by some twenty degrees."
"10131","Al-Abbas ibn al-Mufaddal al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Insulting the Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"10132","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but he is my brother and my companion, and Allah has taken your companion as a close friend."
"10133","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughira, from Wasil ibn Hayyan, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but your companion is the close friend of Allah; and the Quran was revealed upon seven letters, and for every verse of it is an outer and an inner."
"10134","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zara, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr was known by the movement of his beard."
"10135","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat al-Kindi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd al-Kindi, from Abu al-Ayan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, from Ibn Masud who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed a polytheist man whose blood has become lawful."
"10136","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal al-Anmati narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd al-Kindi, from Abu al-Ayan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami, from Ibn Masud who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about apes and pigs: Are they from the offspring of the Jews? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty never cursed a people and transformed them and made for them offspring so they survive; but this was a creation that existed, and when Allah Almighty became angry at the Jews He transformed them and made them like them."
"10137","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Humayd al-Kindi, from Abu al-Jarud, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, raising it, he said: Let not the broad forearms with blood impress you; for it has with Allah a killer who does not die; and let not a man who earned wealth unlawfully impress you; if he spends of it it is not accepted from him, if he withholds it is not blessed for him, and if he dies leaving it it will be his provision to the Fire."
"10138","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever will be reckoned on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, until he says: O Lord, relieve me even to the Fire."
"10139","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath deliberately to cut off the wealth of a Muslim man without right will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him. And he recited: Indeed those who buy with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price, the verse. Yazid ibn Ibrahim raised it, and Hammad ibn Zayd did not raise it."
"10140","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: Whoever swears a binding oath deliberately therein sinfully to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"10141","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Qatada, from Muwarriq al-Ijli, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The woman is private (awra); when she goes out Satan looks at her; she is nearest to Allah while in the depth of her house."
"10142","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba al-Asqalani narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Abdi narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Fazara, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to read in the Fajr prayer on Friday Alif Lam Mim, the revelation, al-Sajda, and Has there come upon man."
"10143","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Firdaws al-Ashari narrated to us, Masud ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hakam narrating, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened the prayer he said: Glory be to You O Allah, and with Your praise, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god besides You."
"10144","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, they said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He who is moderate never becomes poor."
"10145","Al-Hasan ibn Alluya al-Qattan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murra, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: That I swear nine times that Ibn Sayyad is the Dajjal is dearer to me than swearing once; and that I swear nine times that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was killed a martyr is dearer to me than swearing once that he was not killed; that is because Allah Almighty made him a prophet and took him as a martyr."
"10146","A chapter. Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying and greeted him, and he did not return it to me; when he finished his prayer he said: Allah Almighty brings about for His Prophet what He wills, and among what He brought about for him is that you not speak in prayer."
"10147","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: We used to speak in prayer; some of us greeted others and one of us gestured for a need. One day I came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying and greeted him, and he did not return it to me; I was seized by what was past and what is new. When he finished he said: Allah Almighty brings about of His command what He wills, and He has brought about that you not speak in prayer."
"10148","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyayna, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wail who said: Ibn Masud said: We used to greet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer and he would return it to us; when I came from the land of Abyssinia I greeted him and he did not return it to us; I was seized by what preceded and what followed. Then I waited for him; when he finished his prayer I mentioned that to him, and he said: Allah brings about of His command what He wills, and He has decreed - or said: brought about - that you not speak in prayer."
"10149","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjulani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah who said: We used to speak in prayer and some of us greeted others, and one of us gestured to his companion for a need. One day I came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying and greeted him, and he did not return it to me; I was seized by what was past and what is new. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished he said: Allah brings about of His command what He wills, and He has brought about that you not speak in prayer."
"10150","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Hammad who said: I thought it was from Abu Wail, or from Ibrahim, Mamar doubted, from Ibn Masud who said: People used to return greetings to one another in prayer, until Ibn Masud greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not return it to him; he sat grieving, imagining something had been revealed concerning him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, Ibn Masud mentioned that to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In prayer there is occupation, and occupation with prayer suffices."
"10151","10125 - Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid reported, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, that he went out to the land of Abyssinia while people were greeting one another in prayer. When Abdullah returned, he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he did not return it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: I seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger; I greeted him and he did not return it to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is indeed preoccupation in prayer."
"10152","10126 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer and he would return it to us. When we returned from the Negus we greeted him and he did not return it to us, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to greet you in prayer and you would return it to us. He said: There is indeed preoccupation in prayer."
"10153","10127 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Abu Khalid narrated, from Shubah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is indeed preoccupation in prayer."
"10154","10128 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated, Ibn Jabir narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Masud reported to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that he used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying and he would return the greeting to him. Then he greeted him while he was praying and he did not return it to him, so Abdullah thought that was due to anger from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he finished he said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to greet you while you were praying and you would return it to me; then I greeted you and you did not return it to me, and I thought that was due to anger against me. He said: No, but we have been forbidden from speech in prayer except with the Quran and remembrance."
"10155","10129 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated, Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from al-Radrad, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We used to greet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer and he would return it to us. One day I greeted him and he did not return it to me, so I asked him about that, and he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, brings about whatever He wills of His affair."
"10156","10130 - Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asim, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Abdullah, he said: We used to speak in prayer, greeting one another, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, brings about whatever He wills of His affair, and He has now brought about that you shall not speak in prayer."
"10157","10131 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, Israil narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: I went out for some need while some of us were greeting others in prayer, then I returned and greeted, but he did not return it to me, and he said: There is indeed preoccupation in prayer."
"10158","The disagreement over al-Amash in the hadith of Abdullah: While I was clinging to the curtains of the Kabah. 10132 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, both saying: Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Wahb ibn Rabiah, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: I was sheltering behind the curtains of the Kabah when three men came: a Thaqafi and his two Qurashi brothers-in-law, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding; they spoke among themselves, and one of them said: Do you think Allah hears what we said? Another said: When we raise our voices He hears, and when we lower them He does not hear. The other said: If He hears when we raise, then He hears when we lower. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {And you did not use to conceal yourselves lest your hearing, your sight, and your skins testify against you, but you thought that Allah does not know much of what you do}, up to His saying: {of the losers}. Thus Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it, and Abu Muawiyah and the companions of al-Amash differed from him."
"10159","10133 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to me, Qabisah narrated, from Qutbah, he said: So-and-so said to al-Amash: Narrate the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid from Abdullah: I was sheltering behind the curtains of the Kabah; Sufyan narrates it from you, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Wahb ibn Rabiah. He said: Al-Amash hummed for a while, then said: It is as Sufyan said."
"10160","10134 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Abdullah said: I was sheltering behind the curtains of the Kabah, when three men came, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding in their hearts: a Qurashi and his two Thaqafi brothers-in-law, or a Thaqafi and his two Qurashi brothers-in-law. They spoke words I did not understand. One of them said: Do you think Allah hears our speech? Another said: When we raise our voices He hears them, and when we do not raise them He does not hear them. The other said: If He hears any of it, He hears all of it. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {And you did not use to conceal yourselves lest your hearing and your sight testify against you}, the verse."
"10161","10135 - al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: I was sheltering behind the curtains of the Kabah, when three men came, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Abu Muawiyah. Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated it, differing from al-Thawri and the companions of al-Amash."
"10162","10136 - Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani and Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Muafa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Kuraymah al-Harrani narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: I was sheltering behind the covering of the Kabah, while in the mosque there was a man of Thaqif and his two Qurashi brothers-in-law. He said: Do you think Allah hears our murmuring? One of them said: He hears when we raise our voices. The other said: If He hears when we raise, He will surely hear when we lower. Ibn Masud said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what they said, and Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {And you did not use to conceal yourselves lest your hearing, your sight, and your skins testify against you}, to the end of the verse. Al-Masudi differed from them."
"10163","10137 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Daqiqi narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, al-Masudi reported, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: While I was sheltering behind the curtains of the Kabah, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah."
"10164","10138 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah,"
"10165","(H) he said: And Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah, he said: Three men sat at the door of the Kabah, two Qurashis and a Thaqafi, or two Thaqafis and a Qurashi, and one of them confided something to another. One of them said: Do you think Allah hears what we say? Some of them said: As for what we utter aloud, He hears it. The other said: If He hears what we utter aloud, then He hears what we conceal. So Allah, blessed and exalted, sent down {And you did not use to conceal yourselves}, the verse."
"10166","10139 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah, the like of it."
"10167","The disagreement over al-Amash in the hadith of Abdullah about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina. 10140 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: It reached Abdullah that Uthman prayed four rakahs at Mina, so Abdullah said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rakahs, two rakahs; and with Abu Bakr two rakahs, two rakahs; and with Umar two rakahs, two rakahs; then the paths diverged with you, so would that my share of four rakahs were two accepted rakahs."
"10168","10141 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Uthman prayed four at Mina, so Abdullah said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr two rakahs, and with Umar two rakahs; then the paths diverged with you, so I wish that for four rakahs I had two accepted rakahs."
"10169","10142 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Ahwal narrated, Abu Ubaydah ibn Man narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr two rakahs, and with Umar two rakahs; then the paths diverged with you."
"10170","10143 - Sulayman ibn al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Musa ibn Ayan narrated, from Idris al-Kufi, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rakahs. Thus the companions of al-Amash narrated it, and Shubah differed from them."
"10171","10144 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah reported, from al-Amash, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr or another narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he prayed at Mina two rakahs; and with Abu Bakr he prayed two rakahs; and with Umar he prayed two rakahs; so would that my share were two accepted rakahs."
"10172","Qays ibn al-Rabi differed from them. 10145 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, at Mina, two rakahs."
"10173","Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Arzami differed from them. 10146 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Jundaysaburi narrated, Ashath ibn Attaf narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Arzami narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr two rakahs, and with Umar two rakahs."
"10174","Israil differed from them. 10147 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Israil narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr two rakahs, and with Umar two rakahs."
"10175","The disagreement over al-Amash in the hadith of Abdullah ibn Masud that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of a snake at Mina. 10148 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad narrated, Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, Abd Allah ibn Masud narrated, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave when there was sent down upon him {By those sent forth in succession}; he said: I was receiving it from his mouth, fresh, and his mouth was moist with it, when a snake came out at us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill it. It escaped us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your harm just as you were protected from its harm."
"10176","10149 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave at Mina when a snake leapt at us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill it. We rushed for it but it outran us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your harm just as you were protected from its harm."
"10177","10150 - al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Ismail ibn Hafs al-Ubulli narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of a snake in the sanctuary."
"10178","10151 - Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of a snake at Mina."
"10179","10152 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave when a snake came out. He said: Kill it. It outran us, and he said: It was protected from your harm just as you were protected from its harm."
"10180","10153 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir and Ibn Idris narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Razin, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: Abdullah said: Al-Mursalat was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were in a cave, and he had me recite it, and I recite it nearly as he had me recite it; I do not know with which of its two endings he concluded: {And when it is said to them: Bow, they do not bow}, or: {Then in what statement after it will they believe}."
"10181","10154 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, when {By those sent forth in succession} was sent down upon him. I took it from his mouth, and his mouth was moist with it. I do not know with which of the two it is concluded: {Then in what statement after it will they believe}, or: {And when it is said to them: Bow, they do not bow}. He said: A snake escaped him into a hole, and he said: You were protected from its harm, and it was protected from your harm."
"10182","10155 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: Abdullah recited {By those sent forth in succession} and said: It was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the snake. We said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the night of the snake? He said: We were with him when a snake came out at us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go after it. We went after it but it defeated us until it entered its hole. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it; Allah has protected it from your harm and protected you from its harm."
"10183","10156 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, Israil narrated, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave when there was sent down upon him: {By those sent forth in succession}; we were receiving it from his mouth while it was moist, when a snake came out at us. We rushed to kill it, but it slipped away, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your harm, and you were protected from its harm."
"10184","10157 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Nafi ibn Yazid narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Mujahid, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: While we were in the mosque of al-Khayf on the night of Arafah, we heard the sound of a snake. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill it. It entered a crack in a hole, so a palm frond was brought and fire was kindled in it, then we cleared part of the hole but did not find it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it; Allah has protected it from your harm and protected you from its harm."
"10185","10158 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, when {By those sent forth} was sent down upon him; then there was a snake, so they sought it but it escaped them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were indeed protected from its harm just as it was protected from your harm."
"10186","10159 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Qabisah narrated, from Warqa, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave when {By those sent forth} was sent down upon him; we were receiving it from his mouth when a snake came out at us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill it. We rushed for it, then it entered its hole, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your harm just as you were protected from its harm."
"10187","10160 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, Shayban narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10188","The disagreement over al-Amash in the hadith of Abdullah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often finished the prayer turning to his left. 10161 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from a man, from al-Aswad, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: Let none of you give Satan a share of himself, nor consider it a duty upon him to turn only to his right; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often turning to his left."
"10189","10162 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: Let none of you give Satan a share of himself, nor consider it anything but a duty upon him not to turn except to his right; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often turning to his left."
"10190","10163 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: Let none of you give Satan a share of himself, nor consider it anything but a duty upon him to turn to his right; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often turning to his left."
"10191","10164 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjulani narrated, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often turning to his left. Thus the companions of al-Amash narrated it, and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah differed from them."
"10192","10165 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Mustawrid al-Ijli, that Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often turning to his left."
"10193","The disagreement over al-Amash in the hadith of Abdullah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is marriage. 10166 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Shubah, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever has means, let him marry; otherwise let him fast, for fasting is a restraint for him."
"10194","10167 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bistam al-Zafaraniyy narrated, Muammil ibn Ismail narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10195","10168 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of youths, whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private parts; and whoever cannot, fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him."
"10196","10169 - al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10197","10170 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated, Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry; and whoever cannot, fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him."
"10198","10171 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: We complained of bachelorhood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Upon you is marriage; whoever cannot, fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him."
"10199","Chapter. 10172 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr and Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, they said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying the takbir with every raising and lowering, standing and sitting, and giving the salutation to his right and his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."
"10200","10173 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, (H) and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and al-Thawri, (H) and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruwasi narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, (H) and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sahban al-Shirazi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan narrated, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated, from Ali ibn Salih, (H) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sharik, (H) and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, (H) and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mikhraq al-Firyabi narrated, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated, Yala ibn Ubayd narrated, my brother Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to me, all of them from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. And the wording is from the hadith of Abu Nuaym from Sufyan."
